('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'litvinenko-inquiry-118', '298', 'The Litvinenko Inquiry'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'restrictions-disclosure-publication-evidence-documents', '298', 'Restrictions on the Disclosure or Publication of Evidence or Documents given, produced or provided to the Inquiry 4 The restrictions referred to at paragraphs 5 and 7 below are imposed:'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'i-being-required-rule-law', '298', '(i) as being required by the rule of law known as public interest immunity; and/or'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'ii-because-minister-acting-accordance', '298', '(ii) because the Minister, acting in accordance with section 19(3)(b) of the Act'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'restrictions-attendance-inquiry-part-inquiry', '298', 'Restrictions on Attendance at the Inquiry or part of the Inquiry 8 The restrictions referred to at paragraphs 9, 12, and 14 below are imposed:'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'i-being-required-rule-law-2', '298', '(i) as being required by the rule of law known as public interest immunity; and/or'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'ii-because-minister-acting-accordance-2', '298', '(ii) because the Minister, acting in accordance with section 19(3)(b) of the Act'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'appendix-7-restriction-notices-orders', '299', 'Appendix 7 | Restriction Notices and Orders indicates in writing that the attendance of the person is necessary, and arrangements are in place which the Minister considers adequate to ensure that the public interest in preventing the disclosure of the Schedule material is not damaged.12 Berezovsky 25/3-30 Marina Litvinenko 4/31-32; 4/41; 4/112-114 INQ019146 (page 22 paragraph 69) INQ021208 (page 6) Elenora Wall 32/81 INQ020031 No person shall produce or show to any witness any of the Schedule material, or ask any questions which tend to reveal the existence or content of such material, otherwise than in accordance with a procedure formulated by the Core Inquiry Team and agreed in writing by the Minister.Show full note No person shall produce or show to any witness any of the Schedule material, or ask any questions which tend to reveal the existence or content of such material, otherwise than in accordance with a procedure formulated by the Core Inquiry Team and agreed in writing by the Minister. The Chairman shall ensure that no transcript of the evidence given at a closed hearing is made available to any person other than the Minister, members of the Core Inquiry Team or HMG advisers.14 Berezovsky 25/6-7 Felshtinsky 23/128-131 Service 28/48 lines 3-9 Hohne 32/51 INQ015781 part 1, INQ015781 part 2; INQ015777 part 1, INQ015777 part 2; INQ015778; INQ015779; INQ015780 [videos] Dombey 23/13-39 The Chairman shall ensure that no reference is made to the substance of the evidence given at a closed hearing of the Inquiry in any open ruling, judgment or report arising out of the Inquiry, or otherwise. Amendments to this Restriction Notice November 2014Show full note The Chairman shall ensure that no reference is made to the substance of the evidence given at a closed hearing of the Inquiry in any open ruling, judgment or report arising out of the Inquiry, or otherwise.'),
('litvinenko-inquiry', 'Appendix 6: Abbreviations', 'amendments-restriction-notice-15-letter', '299', 'Amendments to this Restriction Notice 15 By letter to the Chairman under this paragraph the Minister may remove from the scope of this Notice any document or information referred to in the Schedule. The Chairman may invite the Minister to amend this Restriction Notice at any time upon providing the Minister with a draft of the proposed amendment and written reasons for it. The Minister may amend this Restriction Notice at any time. July 2014 (as amended 21 January 2015)'),
