('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'r3-3-2-initiate-program-designed-2', '225', 'R3.3-2 Initiate a program designed to increase the'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'r3-3-1-develop-implement-comprehensive-2', '225', 'R3.3-1 Develop and implement a comprehensive inspec-'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'r6-4-1-missions-international-space-2', '225', 'R6.4-1 For missions to the International Space Station,'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'carbon-taking-advantage-additional-capabilities', '225', 'Carbon, taking advantage of the additional capabilities available when near to or docked at the International Space Station.'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'non-station-missions-develop-comprehensive-autonomous', '225', 'For non-Station missions, develop a comprehensive autonomous (independent of Station) inspection and repair capability to cover the widest possible range of damage scenarios.'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'accomplish-on-orbit-thermal-protection-system', '225', 'Accomplish an on-orbit Thermal Protection System inspection, using appropriate assets and capabilities, early in all missions.'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'ultimate-objective-should-be-fully', '225', 'The ultimate objective should be a fully autonomous capability for all missions to address the possibility that an International Space Station mission fails to achieve the correct orbit, fails to dock successfully, or is damaged during or after undocking. [RTF]'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'order-understand-true-material-characteristics', '225', 'In order to understand the true material characteristics of Reinforced Carbon-Carbon components, develop a comprehensive database of flown Reinforced Carbon-Carbon material characteristics by destructive testing and evaluation.'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'improve-maintenance-launch-pad-structures', '225', 'Improve the maintenance of launch pad structures to minimize the leaching of zinc primer onto Reinforced Carbon-Carbon components.'),
('columbia-accident', 'PART ONE – THE ACCIDENT', 'obtain-sufficient-spare-reinforced-carbon-carbon', '225', 'Obtain sufficient spare Reinforced Carbon-Carbon panel assemblies and associated support components to ensure that decisions on Reinforced Carbon-Carbon maintenance are made on the basis of component specifications, free of external pressures relating to schedules, costs, or other considerations.'),
