('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'january-2000-ronald-w-ferrier', '315', '(January 2000).97 Ibid. Commission staff analysis of Bureau of Ocean Energy Management, Regulation and Enforcement data; Minerals Management Service, U.S. Offshore Milestones (as of August 2006): 5. See http://www.boemre.gov/stats/PDFs/ milestonesAUG2006.pdf. Keith, interview. Given what we now know, it is all but impossible that the well was not flowing as of 9:08 p.m. BP, Deepwater Horizon Accident Investigation Report, 25; Smith, Review of Operational Data Preceding Explosion on Deepwater Horizon, 22–23. Other than faulty memory, the only apparent explanations for Mr. Keith''s statement are that the crew had already closed off the portion of the flow line Mr. Keith was watching or that Mr. Keith watched for an inadequate period of time. Keith, interview; Darryl Bourgoyne (LSU), interview with Commission staff, No- vember 23, 2010. Exxon Mobil, 2009 Corporate Citizenship Report, 14.Show full note Ronald W. Ferrier, The History of the British Petroleum Company, Vol. 1: The Developing Years, 1901–1932 (Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1982); J.H. Bamberg, The History of British Petroleum, Vol. 2: The Anglo-Iranian Years, 1928–1945 (Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1994); and James Bamberg, British Petroleum and'),
