('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'interview-government-official-september-15', '329', 'Interview with government official, September 15, 2010. Interview with Coast Guard official, August 31, 2010.62 Ibid.; Testimony of Andrea Fleytas, Hearing before the Deepwater Horizon Joint Investigation Team, October 5, 2010, 16; Testimony of Daun Winslow, August 23, 2010, 296. National Research Council Committee on Marine Area Governance and Management, Striking a Balance: Improving Stewardship of Marine Areas (Washington, D.C.: National Academy of Sciences, 1997), 37, http://www.nap.edu/ openbook.php?record_id=5797&page=37. Internal BP document (BP-HZN-CEC 21260-279).Show full note Interview with BP official, October 22, 2010; Interview with government official, October 5, 2010; Interview with government official, August 24, 2010; Interview with Coast Guard official, August 25, 2010. La. Rev. Stat. § 29: 727. Interview with government official, October 8, 2010. Interview with Coast Guard official, October 20, 2010.66 Ibid., 282. Jan Erik Vinnem, Offshore Risk Assessment: Principles, Modelling and Applications of QRA Studies, 2nd ed. (London: Springer Studies in Reliability Engineering, 2007), 91, 100, 102. The blind shear rams closed and sealed as expected during the positive-pressure test. This fact suggests that the rams were capable of sealing the well when the blowout occurred. But the evidence is inconclusive on its own; during the positive-pressure test the crew closed the blind shear rams using a low pressure hydraulic system, rather than the high pressure hydraulic system that would have activated the rams in the event of a blowout.Show full note Interview with government official, October 8, 2010; Interview with government official, October 14, 2010. Testimony of Admiral Thad Allen, National Incident Commander, Hearing before the National Commission, September 27, 2010. Press Release, In Precautionary Move, LDWF and DHH Announce Closures Due to Oil Spill, April 30