('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'denmark-including-faroe-islands-greenland', '355', 'Denmark (including the Faroe Islands and Greenland), Finland, Iceland, Norway, the Russian Federation, Sweden, and the United States of America. The Permanent Participants of the Arctic Council are: Aleut International Association (AIA), Arctic Athabaskan Council (AAC), Gwich''in Council International (GCI), Inuit Circumpolar Council (ICC), Russian Association of Indigenous Peoples of the North (RAIPON), and the Saami Council.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', '356-appendix', '355', '356 Appendix A'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'appendix-a', '355', 'Appendix A'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'commission-members-2', '355', 'Commission Members'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'appendix-357-357', '355', 'Appendix A 357 — 357'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'donald-f-boesch-member-president', '355', 'DONALD F. BOESCH, Member, is President of the University of Maryland Center for Environmental Science, where he is also a Professor of Marine Science and Vice Chancellor for Environmental Sustainability for the University System of Maryland. He is a biological oceanographer who has conducted research on coastal ecosystems along the Atlantic Coast, the Gulf of Mexico, Australia and the East China Sea. A native of Louisiana, he has assessed the long-term environmental effects of offshore oil and gas development and multiple environmental problems of the Gulf Coast.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'terry-d-garcia-member-currently', '355', 'TERRY D. GARCIA, Member, is currently Executive Vice President for Mission Programs for the National Geographic Society, responsible for the Society''s core programs that manage more than 400 scientific field research, conservation and exploration projects annually. From 1994 to 1996, he was General Counsel at NOAA and led the implementation of the Exxon Valdez Oil Spill Restoration Plan for Prince William Sound and the Gulf of Alaska. From 1997 to 1999, he was Assistant Secretary of Commerce for Oceans and Atmosphere and Deputy Administrator of NOAA.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'cherry-murray-member-dean-harvard', '355', 'CHERRY A. MURRAY, Member, is Dean of the Harvard School of Engineering and Applied Sciences and John A. and Elizabeth S. Armstrong Professor of Engineering and Applied Sciences. She is currently the Past President of the American Physical Society. She was formerly Senior Vice President of Physical Science & Wireless Research at Bell Labs and past Principal Associate Director for Science & Technology at Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory. A member of the National Academy of Engineering and the National Academy of Sciences, she has served on more than 80 national and international scientific advisory committees, governing boards, and National Research Council panels, including chairing the Council''s Division of Engineering and Physical Science.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'fran-ulmer-member-chancellor-university', '355', 'FRAN ULMER, Member, is Chancellor of the University of Alaska Anchorage, Alaska''s largest public university. Ms. Ulmer has served as Mayor of Juneau and Lieutenant Governor of Alaska. As a state legislator, she served on the Special Committee on the Exxon Valdez Oil Spill Claims Settlement. She has been a member of the North Pacific Anadromous Fish Commission, the Alaska Coastal Policy Council, the Alaska Nature Conservancy, the National Parks Conservation Association, the Aspen Institute''s Commission on Arctic Climate Change, among many others.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', '358-appendix-b', '355', '358 Appendix B'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'appendix-b', '355', 'Appendix B'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'list-acronyms', '355', 'List of Acronyms'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'appendix-c-359-359', '355', 'Appendix C 359 — 359'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'appendix-c', '355', 'Appendix C'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'executive-order---national-commission-bp', '355', 'Executive Order-- National Commission on the BP Deepwater Horizon Oil Spill and Offshore Drilling'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'authority-vested-me-president-constitution', '355', 'By the authority vested in me as President by the Constitution and the laws of the United States of America, it is hereby ordered as follows:'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'section-1-establishment-there-established', '355', 'Section 1. Establishment. There is established the National Commission on the BP Deepwater Horizon Oil Spill and Offshore Drilling (the "Commission").'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'sec-2-membership-commission-shall', '355', 'Sec. 2. Membership. (a) The Commission shall be composed of not more than 7 members who shall be appointed by the President. The members shall be drawn from among distinguished individuals, and may include those with experience in or representing the scientific, engineering, and environmental communities, the oil and gas industry, or any other area determined by the President to be of value to the Commission in carrying out its duties.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'b-president-shall-designate-from', '355', '(b) The President shall designate from among the Commission members two members to serve as Co Chairs.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'sec-3-mission-commission-shall', '355', 'Sec. 3. Mission. The Commission shall:'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'examine-relevant-facts-circumstances-concerning', '355', '(a) examine the relevant facts and circumstances concerning the root causes of the'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'deepwater-horizon-oil-disaster', '355', 'Deepwater Horizon oil disaster;'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'b-develop-options-guarding-against', '355', '(b) develop options for guarding against, and mitigating the impact of, oil spills associated with offshore drilling, taking into consideration the environmental, public health, and economic effects of such options, including options involving:'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', '1-improvements-federal-laws-regulations', '355', '(1) improvements to Federal laws, regulations, and industry practices applicable to'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', '2-organizational-other-reforms-federal', '355', '(2) organizational or other reforms of Federal agencies or processes necessary to ensure such improvements are implemented and maintained.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'c-submit-final-public-report', '355', '(c) submit a final public report to the President with its findings and options for consideration within 6 months of the date of the Commission''s first meeting.'),
('us-deepwater-horizon', 'ENDNOTES', 'sec-4-administration-commission-shall', '355', 'Sec. 4. Administration. (a) The Commission shall hold public hearings and shall request information including relevant documents from Federal, State, and local officials, nongovernmental organizations, private entities, scientific institutions, industry and'),
