('us-v-philip-morris', 'Elliott; Engineered Energy Mgt. Inc.; Environmental Policy Institute; J. Earle Estes; Frederick', '503646200-6200-us-29701-01335767-5772-us', '179', '503646200-6200 (US 29701); 01335767-5772 (US 26506); 01335774-5774 (US 26507); 01335761- 5764 (US 26505); 980078407-8411 (US 25865). See Section III(E)(3)(d), infra, for discussion of the Harvard/Huber research.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Elliott; Engineered Energy Mgt. Inc.; Environmental Policy Institute; J. Earle Estes; Frederick', 'f-committees', '179', 'F. Committees'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Research Review Committee, Research Liaison Committee, and Industry', 'committee-should-be-established-review', '179', 'committee should be established to review their support of medical research and to make recommendations as to the future course Defendants'' support should take. At a CTR meeting, Lorillard, through its President Curtis Judge, agreed to participate in an increased budget for CTR only on condition that such a review of industry research be undertaken. BWX0007549-7588 (US 86832); ARU1130828-0904 (US 86773).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Research Review Committee, Research Liaison Committee, and Industry', 'lwodj9055531-5532-us-26009-confidential-2015040862-0863', '181', 'LWODJ9055531-5532 (US 26009) (Confidential); 2015040862-0863 (US 36652); ZN22408-2408 (US 86391); CTR98CONG01187-1189 (US 21137); 03540217-0225 (US 22294); LWODJ9055501- 5505 (US 25957) (Confidential); 03659013-9016 (US 29300).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Research Review Committee, Research Liaison Committee, and Industry', 'industry-representatives-held-meetings-reported', '182', 'Industry representatives held meetings and reported to the companies'' General Counsels. The name of this new committee was the Industry Research Committee, which essentially performed the same functions as the prior Research Liaison Committee. 01346204-6205 (US 34532) (emphasis in original); Stevens WD, 29:20-38:15; 95539849-9850 (US 56829); TIOK0032721-2722 (US 63003);'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Research Review Committee, Research Liaison Committee, and Industry', 'bwx0007531-7548-us-36238', '183', 'BWX0007531-7548 (US 36238).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Research Review Committee, Research Liaison Committee, and Industry', '680212421-2423-us-54024-682338651-8653-us', '183', '680212421-2423 (US 54024); 682338651-8653 (US 22899).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', '682011463-1466-us-86418-1001609316-9320-us', '185', '682011463-1466 (US 86418); 1001609316-9320 (US 86419).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', 'committee-present-again-meeting-representatives', '185', 'Committee." Present again at the meeting were representatives from CTR, American, B&W,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', 'reynolds-lorillard-philip-morris-chadbourne', '185', 'Reynolds, Lorillard, Philip Morris, and Chadbourne & Parke.');
INSERT INTO passages (report, section, paragraph_id, page, body) VALUES
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', 'atx300008549-8551-us-58614', '185', 'ATX300008549-8551 (US 58614).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', 'b-w-lorillard-philip-morris', '185', 'B&W, Lorillard, Philip Morris, Reynolds, and American attended the meeting. The meeting was called "to hear presentations by the CTR-staff of the contract research program being proposed by'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', 'mason-research-institute-which-involve', '185', 'Mason Research Institute," which was to involve large-scale, long-term mouse inhalation experiments. 955033996-4012 (US 32363). It was noted that:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', '955033996-4012-us-32363-emphasis-original', '186', '955033996-4012 (US 32363) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', '32364', '186', '32364).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', 'morris-preston-leake-american-alexander', '186', 'Morris; Preston Leake of American; Alexander Spears of Lorillard; Murray Senkus of Reynolds;'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Industry Technical Committee', 'william-w-bates-liggett-i', '186', 'William W. Bates of Liggett; and I.W. Hughes of B&W -- expressed their displeasure with CTR''s research program, its focus on studies of diseases that were associated with smoking, its defensive posture, and its lack of guidance for future strategy of the tobacco industry in the area of smoking and health. The report offered opinions as to how CTR might become more effective as an instrument for the good of the tobacco industry. 1002636362-6365 (US 22998).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tobacco Working Group', 'hhs1330992-0998-us-76082', '189', 'HHS1330992-0998 (US 76082).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tobacco Working Group', '01240178-0178-us-22282', '189', '01240178-0178 (US 22282).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tobacco Working Group', 'timn0081403-1405-us-77050', '192', 'TIMN0081403-1405 (US 77050).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Coordinated Smoking and Health Literature Collection and Retrieval', 'although-each-cigarette-company-handled', '194', 'Although each cigarette company handled its own litigation through various trial attorneys,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Coordinated Smoking and Health Literature Collection and Retrieval', '80684691-4695-us-21067', '194', '80684691-4695 (US 21067).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Organizations Focused on ETS Issues', '20169-us-75204-500294698-4698-us', '199', '20169), (US 75204); 500294698-4698 (US 24145); 504126505-6507 (US 24216); 03638976-8979 (US 46483); 01337388-7388 (US 86504). Regular members of this committee, sometimes referred to as the Public Smoking Committee or Advisory Group, included company scientists from Reynolds, Philip Morris, B&W, and Lorillard. 1000125386-5386 (US 86505); 504339411-9412 (US 86506).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'International Organizations, Committees, and Groups', 'economic-interests-would-best-be', '200', 'economic interests would best be served by pursuing a united front on smoking and health issues and by a global coordination of their activities to protect and enhance their market positions in their respective countries. To further their shared objectives, the Defendants, over an extended period of time, created, controlled, used, or participated in an astonishing array of international entities, including, among many others (all of which will be discussed infra), the Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee ("TMSC"), which became the Tobacco Research Council ("TRC") and then the Tobacco Advisory Council ("TAC"); the International Committee on Smoking Issues ("ICOSI"), which became the International Tobacco Information Center, Inc. ("INFOTAB") and then the International Tobacco Documentation Center ("TDC"); and the Center for Cooperation in Scientific Research Relative to Tobacco/Centre de Coopération pour les Recherches Scientifiques Relatives au Tabac ("CORESTA").'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'International Organizations, Committees, and Groups', '800123779-3782-3781-us-89137', '204', '800123779-3782 at 3781 (US 89137).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'International Organizations, Committees, and Groups', '1003717317-7330-7318-us-86518-emphasis', '204', '1003717317-7330 at 7318 (US 86518) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'International Organizations, Committees, and Groups', '502429369-9373-us-29556-ti16740660-0663-us', '205', '502429369-9373 (US 29556); TI16740660-0663 (US 72403); 2501029891-9901 (US 20557); TI04962210-2211 (US 67250); see also 1002610069-0069 (US 86541).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', 'tlt0900159-0161-us-87720-arrangement-which', '207', 'TLT0900159-0161 (US 87720). The arrangement by which Campbell-Johnson would "act as liaison through which the British industry could clear information regarding developments which it desired to communicate to TIRC" was confirmed by Timothy Hartnett when he was in London later in the spring of 1954. TLT0902041-2064 at 2060 (US 88360).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', 'its-stated-purpose', '208', 'Its stated purpose was'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', 'geoffrey-f-todd-appointed-director', '208', 'Geoffrey F. Todd was appointed Director of TMSC. Alan Campbell-Johnson, Hill & Knowlton''s London associate, was appointed public relations consultant to TMSC. TSMC occupied a position in the United Kingdom analogous to the position of TIRC in the United States. 110070785-0842 at 0788-0789 (US 20270); TLT0900822-0825 (87725); (no bates) (JD 011382); Read TT, 3/21/05, 16327:25-16328:14.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', '093292', '209', '093292).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', 'england-meet-tmsc-members-june', '209', 'England to meet with TMSC members in June 1956, Campbell-Johnson wrote to John Hill that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', 'hartnett-s-presence-particular-moment', '209', 'Hartnett''s "presence at that particular moment should do much materially to help to get relations between TIRC and the new committee [TMSC] off to a good start." Campbell-Johnson ended the letter by counseling that:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', 'tlt0900822-0825-us-87725', '209', 'TLT0900822-0825 (US 87725).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TMSC – Tobacco Manufacturers'' Standing Committee', 'ctr-tirc-min000001-0252-0183-jd-093292', '210', 'CTR-TIRC-MIN000001-0252 at 0183 (JD 093292).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TRC – Tobacco Research Council', 'tt-10-18-04-2752', '211', 'TT, 10/18/04, 2752:11-14; Henningfield TT, 11/29/04, 7204:14-19; 321310317-0342 (JD 031027); Read TT, 3/21/05, 16329:5-9.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TRC – Tobacco Research Council', 'one-meetings-philip-morris-t', '211', 'At one of the meetings with Philip Morris, "[t]he informal agreement between TRC members not to make health claims was explained." 1003119099-9135 at 9106, 9108, 9115 (US 20152); Read TT, 3/21/05, 16335:11-14.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TRC – Tobacco Research Council', '680204115-4117-us-20990-read-tt', '212', '680204115-4117 (US 20990); Read TT, 3/21/05, 16335:1-10, 16335:17-16336:5.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', '7277-18-23-see-also-300545676-5680', '213', '7277:18-23; see also 300545676-5680 (US 87579); 300543360-3366 (US 88545); 800123779-3782'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', 'meeting-smoking-health-stated', '213', 'Meeting on Smoking and Health, stated that:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', '301043570-3571-us-93210-read-tt', '213', '301043570-3571 (US 93210); Read TT, 3/22/05, 16406:24-16408:24.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', 'participants-agreed-replace-summaries-results', '213', 'The participants agreed to replace summaries of the results of grantees'' research -- which the researchers had written -- with "much shorter statements of results prepared by TAC and agreed to by the grantees." 109840381-0383 at 0383 (US 20261).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', 'memorandum-further-pointed-out-members', '214', 'The memorandum further pointed out that members of the TAC were'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', 'green-requested-permission-from-rjr', '214', 'Green requested permission from RJR to attend the meetings as "the value of our participation in these meetings should be obvious." Handwritten comments on the typed memorandum read:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', '508192982-2982-us-86533-1986-mary', '214', '508192982-2982 (US 86533). In 1986, Mary Ward served as Assistant Counsel in RJR''s R&D Department. Ward WD, 2:13-19.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', 'memorandum-further-stated', '215', 'This memorandum further stated that:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TAC -- Tobacco Advisory Council', 'proposed-follow-up-meeting-purpose-generating', '216', 'A proposed follow-up meeting "with the purpose of generating a world-wide ETS action plan" is further described. 508226799-6804 (US 75279); Ward WD, 71:17-72:6, 72:10-73:17.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', 'proposed-agenda-meeting-included', '218', 'The proposed agenda for the meeting included'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', 'defendants-effort-ultimately-termed-operation', '218', 'Defendants'' effort was ultimately termed "Operation Berkshire" (discussed further at Section V(G)(6)(a)((2)), infra). 2025025347-5348 (US 75149); 2025025286-5286 (US 20407); 2025025290-5291 (US 22980); 2025025347-5348 (US 20410).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', '2025048998-9014-8999-us-20412-see', '219', '2025048998-9014 at 8999 (US 20412); see also 503143820-4106 at 3909 (US 75974).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', 'garrett-attended-representatives-major-united', '219', 'Garrett, was attended by representatives of the major United States tobacco manufacturing companies. The meeting participants jointly agreed to "hold the line on admissions concerning what they would admit to their individual governments concerning smoking and health, among other things." Harris TT, 10/14/04, 2576:10-24, 2577:11-18; see also 2025025295-5300 (US 75146).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', 'according-notes-batco-s-files', '219', 'According to notes in BATCo''s files from a March 1978 meeting in Australia, the objective of'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', 'icosi-defensive-research-aimed-throwing', '219', 'ICOSI was "defensive research aimed at throwing up a smoke screen and to throw doubts on smoking research findings which show smoke causes deceases [sic]." 321588692-8692 (US 28544).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', '1981-tobacco-institute-college-tobacco', '219', '1981 Tobacco Institute College of Tobacco Knowledge in Washington, D.C. that the organization'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', 'first-named-icosi-later-renamed', '220', '(first named ICOSI and later renamed INFOTAB) was founded to perform internationally the functions that the Tobacco Institute performed for the domestic industry in the United States: "From the outset, the members recognized that the social acceptability of smoking, including the public smoking issue was a subject on which attention should be focused [sic]." 2501029891-9901 at 9896 (US 20557); see also TI04962210-2210 (US 67250); Blackie TT, 10/26/04, 3846:18-22.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'ICOSI – International Committee on Smoking Issues', 'eec-task-force-consumerism-had', '222', 'EEC Task Force on Consumerism had to prepare an industry response to the EEC Consumer Consultative Committee''s anti-smoking paper "Tobacco and the Health of the Consumer" and suggested that ICOSI members and their respective law firms work together on a common approach to the response, given their exposure to the situation in Europe over the years. 2501025098-5099 (US 86515); 2501025100-5100 (US 86516); 2501025108-5108 (US 86517).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'INFOTAB – International Tobacco Information Center', '504934906-4953-us-20737', '225', '504934906-4953 (US 20737).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'INFOTAB – International Tobacco Information Center', '2015007199-7207-7204-7205-us-20311', '226', '2015007199-7207 at 7204-7205 (US 20311).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'INFOTAB – International Tobacco Information Center', 'organization-tactics-suggested-included-following', '226', 'Organization]. The tactics it suggested included the following:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'INFOTAB – International Tobacco Information Center', 'document-also-suggested-industry-should', '226', 'The document also suggested the industry should attack IOCU [the International Organization of'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'INFOTAB – International Tobacco Information Center', 'consumer-unions-following-program-goals', '226', 'Consumer Unions] with the following program goals: "Relieve NGO pressure on WHO, Expose activists'' ''credentials,'' Counter ''behaviourist'' regulation, correct anti-business slant." 2021595753- 5910 at 5769, 5897, 5903 (US 85541).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TDC – Tobacco Documentation Centre', '301159092-9101-jd-031017-301159136-9151-jd', '228', '301159092-9101 (JD 031017); 301159136-9151 (JD 031018); 700495549-5561 at 5550 (JD 031478); Proctor PD, United States, 6/12/02, 16:8-18, 113:7-11; Tully PD; United States, 6/13/02, 38:9-24.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'TDC – Tobacco Documentation Centre', '502601564-1567-1565-us-29570', '229', '502601564-1567 at 1565 (US 29570).'),
