('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Were Well Aware that Smoking and Nicotine Are Addictive', '1042-supra-section-v-e', '444', '1042), supra, and Section V(E)(2)(b)(2215), infra. In this earlier paper, Dr. Creighton stated that the company''s knowledge of compensation by smokers of low nicotine yield cigarettes came from research "carried out in Hamburg, Montreal, and Southampton within the company," research showing that "smokers do change their smoking patterns in response to changes in the machine smoked deliveries of cigarettes." 105553905-3915 at 3906 (US 34799).'),
