('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'product-manager-t-m-keane', '871', 'Product Manager, to T.M. Keane, Senior Product Manager, stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '980355176-5177-us-85122', '872', '980355176-5177 (US 85122).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '6-lorillard', '872', '(6) Lorillard'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'inc-assist-lorillard-understanding-attitudes', '872', 'Inc., "to assist Lorillard in understanding the . . . attitudes of reduced-tar smokers and their motivations in selecting brands" relayed smokers'' beliefs that lower tar cigarettes had an unsatisfying lack of taste, and indicated that a low tar cigarette "with good taste" had not yet been developed, stating:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '03297227-7249-7229-7233-7246-us', '873', '03297227-7249 at 7229, 7233, 7246 (US 88631).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '03297227-7249-7240-us-88631', '873', '03297227-7249 at 7240 (US 88631).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'cigarette-smoking-tobacco-industry-1978', '873', 'Cigarette Smoking and the Tobacco Industry in 1978 Volume I," prepared for the Tobacco Institute by the Roper Organization stated that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '501565967-6019-6008-us-21866', '873', '501565967-6019 at 6008 (US 21866).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'purportedly-less-harmful-cigarettes-draw', '873', 'purportedly less harmful cigarettes to draw them back into the market and to dissuade potential quitters from actually quitting. According to Carolyn Levy, who worked as a research scientist for Philip Morris in its Behavioral Research Group from 1975-1980 and as the Assistant Director and later Director of Consumer Research from 1986-1991, when she was in the Consumer Research Department, she "performed research on quitting on behalf of Philip Morris," and when she was in the Behavioral Research Department in the late 1970s, "[q]uitting was also a subject of interest and research to Philip Morris."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'rich-greene-inc-regarding-benson', '875', 'Rich, Greene, Inc. regarding Benson & Hedges stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '1004888470-8484-8480-us-85009', '875', '1004888470-8484 at 8480 (US 85009).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2040066740-6766-6747-6751-52-6754-6755', '875', '2040066740-6766 at 6747, 6751-52, 6754, 6755 (US 20435).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2049455309-5318-5313-us-22218-bonhomme', '875', '2049455309-5318 at 5313 (US 22218); Bonhomme WD, 25:15-26:1, 46:19-47:7.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2050801835-1853-1845-us-38763-bonhomme', '877', '2050801835-1853 at 1845 (US 38763); Bonhomme TT, 2/10/05, 12936:6-12939:7.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2072622442-2451-2444-2445-2449-us', '878', '2072622442-2451 at 2444, 2445, 2449 (US 41562); see also 2063688212-8284 at 8226 (US 39823) (Jan. 18, 1994 document prepared for Philip Morris USA indicating that Merit is perceived as a "quitters brand"); Bonhomme WD, 41:4-44:5.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2071032180-2206-2188-us-21964-bible', '878', '2071032180-2206 at 2188 (US 21964); Bible PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 8/22/02, 163:8- 165:2.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2045628312-8328-8320-8326-us-22217', '879', '2045628312-8328 at 8320, 8326 (US 22217).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2080929561-9562-9561-us-27786', '880', '2080929561-9562 at 9561 (US 27786).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '3-r-j-reynolds', '880', '(3) R.J. Reynolds'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 's-group-filter-cigarette-smokers', '880', '"[a]s a group filter cigarette smokers were more conscious of a possible relationship between smoking and health," and recognized the "willingness of an increasing number of smokers to compromise -- to smoke what they considered to be a less harmful cigarette rather than give up smoking entirely." 650340129-0193 at 0180, 0183 (US 20948).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'limit-will-satisfy-needs-smokers', '881', '"LIMIT will satisfy the needs of smokers who wish for the ultimate in low ''tar'' assurance -providing the strongest health reassurances available in cigarettes today." Under the heading "Target'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'audience-memorandum-stated', '882', 'Audience," the memorandum stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '502784092-4100-4097-us-22153-schindler', '882', '502784092-4100 at 4097 (US 22153); Schindler WD, 77:11-78:11.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '500672011-2172-2069-us-20645', '882', '500672011-2172 at 2069 (US 20645).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '500251567-1570-1567-1569-us-21563', '883', '500251567-1570 at 1567-1569 (US 21563).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '503972013-2063-2038-us-66448-orlowsky', '883', '503972013-2063 at 2038 (US 66448); Orlowsky WD, 86:4-7.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'report-further-stated', '884', 'The report further stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '506671319-1418-1326-1379-us-22160', '884', '506671319-1418 at 1326, 1379 (US 22160); Orlowsky WD, 85:8-19.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '650510607-0607-us-87138-smith-wd', '885', '650510607-0607 (US 87138); Smith WD, 63:10-64:7.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '774138538-8545-8539-us-54613', '885', '774138538-8545 at 8539 (US 54613).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'blumenthal-discussed-marketing-strategies-proposed', '885', 'Blumenthal discussed marketing strategies for a proposed new B&W brand pursuant to its "Project'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'omega-report-stated-objective-all', '885', 'Omega." The report stated: "The objective of all advertising and promotion will be to convince low'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'tar-smokers-new-brand-only', '885', '''tar'' smokers that this new brand is the only one that combines the two most important qualities a contemporary cigarette should have -- a satisfying taste and the lowest ''tar.''" The report further stated, under the heading "Conclusions":'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'report-further-stated-these-executions', '886', 'The report further stated: "These executions are built on an expanded strategy which includes an understanding of the target audience and the need to create a maximum ease or comfort level that addresses the concept of ''cognitive dissonance.''" 660026713-6718 at 6714, 6717-6718 (US 85030); Smith WD, 64:19-65:14.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'statements-from-young-smokers-included', '886', 'Statements from young smokers included: "I think all the stuff coming out the past couple of years about how bad smoking is for you made a lot of people go down to a light cigarette to sort of ease their own conscience." 566627751-7824 at 7817-7818 (US 20938).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'those-who-switched-lights-ultras', '887', '"those who switched to lights/ultras because they were attempting to quit." It also noted that some consumers "started smoking lights after making an attempt to quit." The document also shows that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'defendants-intended-their-claims-reduced', '887', 'Defendants intended that their claims of reduced harm regarding low tar cigarettes lessen the social pressure on smokers to quit:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '190200047-0116-0061-0071-0106-us', '887', '190200047-0116 at 0061, 0071, 0106 (US 22162); Ivey WD, 59:1-10.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'inc-titled-topline-report-findings', '887', 'Inc., titled "Topline Report of Findings for Carlton Advertising Research," reported that smokers view Carlton cigarettes as a less harmful alternative to quitting smoking:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'summary-most-common-perceptions-images', '887', 'A "summary of the most common perceptions/images associated with" Carlton and Merit Ultra Light included descriptions of Carlton as for "[s]omeone trying to quit/cut back/smoke lighter" and descriptions of Merit Ultra Light as a "[c]igarette used to quit smoking/almost ready to quit/cutting back." Among the Report''s "Key Findings" were the statements from the focus groups describing their perceptions of several Carlton campaigns. The statements included:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '250255336-5347-5339-5343-47-us-22031', '888', '250255336-5347 at 5339, 5343-47 (US 22031). These statements were repeated in an August 8,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '2000-document-prepared-b-w', '888', '2000 document prepared for B&W by Kay Harwood, Marketing Analysts, Inc., titled "Carlton'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'advertising-research-report-key-findings', '888', 'Advertising Research: Report of Key Findings." 250255060-5075 (US 22170); Ivey WD, 60:1362:22; Smith WD, 62:9-63:6.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '5-batco', '888', '(5) BATCo'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '109883112-3117-3115-3117-us-20264', '888', '109883112-3117 at 3115, 3117 (US 20264); 105657908-7909 (US 20248).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '109883101-3103-3101-3102-us-21518', '889', '109883101-3103 at 3101, 3102 (US 21518).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'cigarettes-quitting-delivered-dr-l', '889', 'Cigarettes and Quitting" and delivered to Dr. L.C.F. Blackman, Director of Millbank, stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '105399687-9689-9688-9689-us-85032', '889', '105399687-9689 at 9688-9689 (US 85032).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'party-stated-smokers-who-are', '889', 'Party" stated: "Smokers who are concerned about the smoking and health aspect but who have not given up, have done all they can (by moving to lower tar brands) to avoid the pressure to quit." The notes continue, recognizing that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '109881462-1467-1462-1463-us-26230', '890', '109881462-1467 at 1462-1463 (US 26230).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'f-william-free-company-advertising-2', '891', 'F. William Free & Company, an advertising agency used by American Tobacco, summarized focus group sessions relating to low tar cigarettes. The report stated: "By changing to a lower tar cigarette, [the panelists] felt less guilty about continuing to smoke and eventually hoped to stop smoking completely." The report stated that "[s]ome of the panelists actually tried smoking brands of low tar in a downward progression of milligrams in order to quit smoking entirely." ATC037310-7324 at'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'atc0136995-7017-7005-7006-us-87906', '892', 'ATC0136995-7017 at 7005, 7006 (US 87906).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'extensive-consumer-research-its-cigarettes', '892', 'extensive consumer research on its cigarettes. For instance, an August 4, 1975 presentation given to Lorillard by a marketing research consultant, titled "Cigarette Advertising 1974-1975," showed that several of the respondents concluded that Lorillard''s "Quit or smoke True" advertisements communicated that True cigarettes are "LESS HARMFUL/BETTER FOR YOU." 03496228-6630 at 6277, 6280 (US 20057).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'under-heading-reasons-prior-brand', '893', 'Under the heading "Reasons for Prior Brand Switching The Switch to SHF," the document stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', '84053616-3706-3618-3628-3632-3637', '893', '84053616-3706 at 3618, 3628, 3632, 3637, 3678-3679 (US 55997).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'report-also-stated-those-who', '894', 'The report also stated: "Those who smoke low tar and nicotine cigarettes generally do so because they believe such cigarettes are ''better for you'' . . . there is less tar and nicotine to do long-term damage . . . reduces smoking anxiety, guilt." 84053709-3744 at 3712-3713, 3716-3719 (US 21073).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Internally Recognized that Smokers Switch to Low', 'liggett-research-department-copeland-robinson', '894', 'Liggett Research Department, to Copeland Robinson, New Products Manager at Liggett, Samfield discussed the importance of releasing Dorset brand cigarettes, citing: "The obvious void in the 4-6 mgm range for a low tar cigarette with acceptable taste. I firmly believe that those who switch to Marvels, Carltons, or Life cigarettes are in the last stages of quitting smoking. The Dorset, however, is a low tar cigarette one can ''live'' with." LWDOJ8006760-6760 (US 87909).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', 'knowledge-compensation-defendants-concealed-knowledge', '894', 'knowledge of compensation, Defendants concealed that knowledge and disseminated false and misleading statements to downplay its existence and prevalence. As part of their attempt to portray low tar cigarettes as less harmful, Defendants publicly endorsed retaining the FTC Method well into the 1990s because of its usefulness to consumers. Henningfield WD, 48:14-49:7; 54:7-15; 55:6-12; 2041186475-6517 at 6475, 6486-95, 6498-04 (US 22181*) (1994 -- B&W, American Tobacco, Lorillard and Liggett defending the validity and usefulness of the FTC Method to consumers);'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', '2048381972-2310-1975-us-22190-521321297-1301', '895', '2048381972-2310 at 1975 (US 22190); 521321297-1301 at 1297 (US 22137); 520011445-1480 at 1445, 1457-58 (US 22101) (1994 -- various public statements by RJR employees defending the validity of the FTC Method); 2505597781-7998B at 7968-87 (US 23028*) (1996 -- Defendants'' statements defending the utility to consumers of the FTC Method).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', '2048381972-2310-2252-2256-us-22190', '898', '2048381972-2310 at 2252, 2256 (US 22190).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', 'tobacco-institute-drafted-december-15', '901', 'of the Tobacco Institute drafted a December 15, 1980 memorandum to Horace Kornegay, President of the Tobacco Institute, warning that, among other issues, the Report was expected to include a discussion of smoker compensation. Rather than recommending disclosure of full and complete information on the subject to the public, the "Response" section of the memorandum stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', 'timn0073798-3799-3799-us-85127', '902', 'TIMN0073798-3799 at 3799 (US 85127).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', 'b-philip-morris', '902', 'b. Philip Morris'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', 'ti01770431-0458-0433-0439-0441-0443-0451', '902', 'TI01770431-0458 at 0433, 0439, 0441-0443, 0451 (US 85065).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants Publicly Denied that', 'atc2746877-6887-6877-6878-6887-us', '903', 'ATC2746877-6887 at 6877, 6878, 6887 (US 59009); compare with 1000861953-1953 (US 35484) (Wakeham 3/24/61) ("As we know, all too often the smoker who switches to a hi-fi cigarette winds up smoking more units in order to provide himself with the delivery which he had before.").'),
