('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'cambridge-consumer-testing-not-required', '926', 'Cambridge: "Consumer testing is not required for this model." Farone WD, 128:23-129:17;'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '1988-you-won-t-miss', '929', '1988: "You Won''t Miss What You''ll Miss." (no bates) (US 8505).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '1988-our-less-your-gain', '929', '1988: "Our Less Is Your Gain." (no bates) (US 8556).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'merit-brand-image-study-noted', '929', '"Merit Brand Image Study," noted in the section "Attitudes Toward Smoking" that "[w]hile health concerns are motivating factor, taste/enjoyment are still key." A summary at the end of the report stated: "Merit smokers we sampled are committed smokers . . . However, they have mixed feelings about smoking -- health concerns/loss of control . . ." and their switching to Merit "provides health reassurance." 2072735414-5500 at 5431, 5492 (US 41598); Bonhomme WD, 27:22-28:17.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'these-smokers-require-most-rational', '931', 'These smokers require the most rational reason why they should smoke Merit, (e.g. lower tar)." Under the heading "Implications," Herman recommended that "[s]ince low tar is essentially the core of these alternative concepts, the low tar message should be more pronounced." 2063724960-4962 at 4960, 4962 (US 39842).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '2041097977-7999-7984-us-85006-bonhomme', '933', '2041097977-7999 at 7984 (US 85006); Bonhomme WD, 31:10-34:17.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '2070624747-4763-4748-us-22014-bonhomme', '934', '2070624747-4763 at 4748 (US 22014); Bonhomme WD, 64:1-6.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'recessed-filter-philip-morris-document', '935', 'a "recessed" filter. A Philip Morris document, titled "Background Information on PM Brands," dated September 1991, stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'benefit-statement-document-parliament-lights', '936', 'A "Benefit Statement" in the document was: "Parliament Lights -- since tar on the filter tip never touches your lips, the taste is refreshingly light." 2070143190-4433 at 3217-3218, 3222 (US 27257).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '4709-see-also-no-bates', '936', '4709); see also (no bates) (US 4885).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'adv029-0247-0249-us-10614', '936', 'ADV029 0247-0249 (US 10614).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'special-filters-minimize-risks-smoking', '936', '"special filters minimize the risks of smoking." FTC, 1981 Report at 2-12 (JD 004744).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'marketing-research-not-just-individual', '937', 'marketing research not just on individual low tar cigarette brands, but on low tar cigarettes as a category. These documents establish that Philip Morris has long known and intended that its advertisements and marketing for low tar cigarettes, featuring claims of lowered tar and nicotine and "light" and "ultra light" brand descriptors, contributed to and reinforced consumers'' mistaken belief that low tar cigarettes are better for their health, and encouraged consumers to smoke them for this reason.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '43-2-43-25-44-2-44', '938', '43:2-43:25; 44:2-44:25; 45:2 - 45:25; 63:10-63:25; 64:2-64:25; 65:2-65:21; 1004888470-8484 (US'),
