('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'see-also-orlowsky-wd-73', '952', 'See also Orlowsky WD, 73:1-76:22 (discussing US 5578; 324; 239; 87456; 87457; and 295);'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '76-23-77-11-discussing-us', '952', '76:23-77:11 (discussing US 6255 ); 77:12-78:21 (discussing US 5756 and 87504); Orlowsky TT,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '10-13-04-2284-14-2285', '952', '10/13/04 2284:14-2285:20 (discussing US 87504).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'both-high-flavor-low-tar', '953', 'both high in flavor and low in ''tar'' and nicotine."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '500713420-3420-us-48350', '953', '500713420-3420 (US 48350).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'vantage-advertisements-stated-rjr-s', '953', 'Vantage advertisements stated that RJR''s advertisement ("Why do you smoke? With what you''ve been hearing about smoking these days, you probably wonder sometimes why you smoke at all") was'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'address-ing-health-issue-competitive', '953', '"address[ing] the health issue for competitive purposes." 690007757-7760 at 7759 (US 21039).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'image-study-k-schmitt-reported', '953', 'Image Study," K.A. Schmitt reported that, based upon the study, "smokers in our target category have two primary product desires: a lower tar product which addresses their safety/health concerns, and a product which provides taste satisfaction." The memorandum further reported that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'vantage-seen-not-dealing-directly', '953', '"VANTAGE is seen as not dealing as directly or effectively with the health/safety concerns of the consumer as Merit. Our current advertising approach focuses much more heavily upon the taste/pleasure aspects of our brand than on the safety/health aspects." As a result, the memorandum recommended that Vantage marketing be modified to better "target" smokers with health concerns:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', 'perhaps-more-balanced-approach-needed', '954', '"Perhaps a more balanced approach is needed, both to tone down the perceptions of harshness and to renew the belief that VANTAGE does indeed address the target consumer''s health/safety concerns." 523474848-4851 at 4848 (US 22156); Orlowsky WD, 71:15-72:16.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '503148009-8077-8006-8070-us-22159', '954', '503148009-8077 at 8006, 8070 (US 22159).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Despite Their Internal Knowledge, Defendants'' Marketing and Public', '511469097-9250-9105-9116-us-20842', '955', '511469097-9250 at 9105, 9116 (US 20842) (emphasis in original); Orlowsky WD, 72:17-23; 81:4-8.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'no-bates-us-5852-1978', '955', '(no bates) (US 5852) (1978); 970469347-9474 at 9430, 9429, 9427, 9431 (US 85104).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'report-went-indicate-when-respondents', '956', 'The report went on to indicate that, when respondents were asked what the words "low" and "lowest" in the advertisements meant to them, "[t]hey interpret this to mean that the two brands are ''safer'' and pose less of a health hazard. Consequently, they reason, this would make the brands more appealing to younger people who are very health conscious or to older, long-time smokers who are concerned about the long-range effects of tobacco." 506671319-1418 at 1379 (US 22160).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'tar-cigarette-brands-low-tar', '956', 'tar cigarette brands, but on low tar cigarettes as a category. These documents demonstrate that RJR has long known and intended that its advertisements and marketing for low tar cigarettes, featuring claims of lowered tar and nicotine and "light" and "ultra light" brand descriptors, contributed to and reinforced consumers'' belief that low tar cigarettes are better for their health, and caused consumers to smoke them for this reason.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'rjr-report-defined-safer-safest', '957', 'The RJR report defined the "Safer" and "Safest" brand categories as follows:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'designated-report-safer-brands-are', '957', '(designated in this report as Safer Brands) are not aware of T&N numbers. Hence, the fact that a'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', '120mm-lights-entry-will-have', '957', '120MM Lights entry will have high T&N numbers (on a total cigarette basis) should not impede its progress." 500671364-1454 at 1408, 1436-37 (US 22158); Schindler WD, 75:5-13.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'document-further-stated-ult-smokers', '959', 'The document further stated: "ULT smokers perceive low tar claims to be credible. They try to balance their desire to smoke and personal concerns." 514343517-3566 at 3522, 3524-26, 3530, 3540 (US 51848).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'persuade-any-nonsmokers-begin-smoking', '959', 'persuade any nonsmokers to begin smoking or in persuading any smokers not to quit." Andrew Schindler, Executive Chairman of Reynolds American Inc., testified that "Reynolds Tobacco is not interested in trying to talk any smokers out of quitting." TLT0770095-0128 (US 72410); Schindler WD, 76:17-77:5.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'tlt0770095-0128-0111-us-72410-schindler', '960', 'TLT0770095-0128 at 0111 (US 72410); Schindler WD, 64:19-65:3.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'kool-must-move-into-health', '960', '"Kool must move into the health reassurance segment so that 45% of KOOL business will be in the perceived product safety arena by 1982 which will approximate the 45% of total smokers who will be smoking hi-fi products by 1982." Under the heading "Strategies," the document stated: "Provide product safety reassurance while enhance [sic] the satisfaction and refreshment perception of the appropriate KOOL styles through the successful national launch in 1979 of either: 1. Low ''tar'' parent [or] 2. Repositioned KOOL Milds." 680559149-9162 at 9149-9150 (US 54048).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'agency-orientation-outline-stating-test', '962', 'Agency Orientation Outline," stating "Test Market Campaigns: Strategy-Given consumers awareness of the smoking and health issue, full flavor smokers must deal with their illogical behavior. Therefore, we attempted to communicate Viceroy''s flavor/satisfaction benefits by providing consumers a rationalization for smoking or a repression of the health concern"); Smith WD, 73:2-17.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'smith-further-explained-those-smokers', '963', 'Smith further explained that, for those smokers, her research has found that their understanding of the tar and nicotine numbers is based "certainly on our advertising." Smith WD, 69:10-14; 75:3-23.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', '250255336-5347-5340-5343-5347-us-22031', '965', '250255336-5347 at 5340, 5343-5347 (US 22031). These statements were repeated in an August 8, 2000 document prepared for B&W by Kay Harwood, Marketing Analysts, Inc. titled "Carlton Advertising Research: Report of Key Findings." 250255060-5075 at 5064, 5066-5068, 5071-5075 (US 22170).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'perceive-health-benefit-brown-williamson', '965', 'they perceive a health benefit," and that "Brown & Williamson''s consumer research . . . indicates that certain smokers switch to low tar cigarettes because they believe that these cigarettes are ''less harmful'' than regular cigarettes." As demonstrated below, these consumer research documents establish that B&W has long known and intended that its advertisements and marketing for low tar cigarettes, featuring claims of lowered tar and nicotine and "light" and "ultra light" brand descriptors, contributed to and reinforced consumers'' mistaken belief that low tar cigarettes are better for their health, and caused consumers to smoke them for this reason.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'ivey-wd-57-22-58-10', '966', 'Ivey WD, 57:22-58:10, 63:1-8; 670186789-6824 at 6790, 6792, 6798, 6802, 6804 (US 21431).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'WHEN IT COMES TO THE LOWEST IN TAR, ONLY ONE', 'world-stated', '966', 'World," stated that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'their-inner-conflicts-about-smoking', '966', 'THEIR INNER CONFLICTS ABOUT SMOKING.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '680282619-2668-2642-us-85305', '966', '680282619-2668 at 2642 (US 85305).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'tobacco-sister-company-b-w', '966', 'Tobacco, the sister company of B&W, stated that the smoker "seeks a new covenant between himself and the tobacco industry" and has "trust" that the industry "is going to provide him with a product that he can enjoy without fear of physical or psychological reprisal." 680082943-3125 at 2959-2960 (US 20983).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '776158413-8426-8416-8419-8422-8423-8425', '968', '776158413-8426 at 8416, 8419, 8422-8423, 8425 (US 22339) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'savannah-brand-be-positioned-against', '969', 'Savannah brand was to be "positioned against those consumers with serious health concerns who continue to smoke full flavor brands." 670156293-6424 at 6303, 6323-6324, 6342 (US 53746*).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'section-titled-market-review-plan', '969', 'In a section titled "Market Review," the plan went on to say that "[t]he appeal of the brands competing in this segment [enriched flavor ultra low tar] is solely on the basis of implied health claims." 670156293-6296 (US 53745); 670156297-6242 at 6324, 6327 (US 53746*).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '1-identification-perceived-underperceived-consumer', '969', '1: Identification of Perceived and Underperceived Consumer Needs," recited the percentage of starters and quitters from 1969-1976, and stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '775036039-6067-6043-6044-6047-6052-us', '969', '775036039-6067 at 6043-6044, 6047, 6052 (US 21053).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '779027336-7360-7339-40-7350-51-7354-55-us', '970', '779027336-7360 at 7339-40, 7350-51, 7354-55 (US 22163).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'products-colleague-don-johnson-discussed', '970', 'Products, to colleague Don Johnson discussed additions to Low Tar Brand Plans. The letter stated that the "Low ''Tar'' Menthol Plan" needed to provide "Health Reassurance." 660093935-3935 (US');
INSERT INTO passages (report, section, paragraph_id, page, body) VALUES
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '53576', '970', '53576).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'reassurance-676038502-8796-8573-8578-8590', '971', 'Reassurance." 676038502-8796 at 8573, 8578, 8590 (US 53923).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '680559100-9124-9100-9101-9110-9120', '971', '680559100-9124 at 9100, 9101, 9110, 9120 (US 21003).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'williamson-tobacco-corp-reported-between', '971', '& Williamson Tobacco Corp.," reported that, between 1974 and 1976, 60-74% of consumers believed that "''low tar and nicotine cigarettes represent a major step in making smoking less harmful.''" Under the heading "''Health'' vs. Image/Taste/Satisfaction," the document stated that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'b-w-s-marketing-plan', '971', 'B&W''s marketing plan included "using acceptably Low Delivery numbers to provide assurance that the brand is at least at parity with its health-oriented competitors." 670133560-3690, 3572, 3581'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'us-53869-document-contains-following', '972', '(US 53869). The document contains the following statements, reflecting B&W''s knowledge that the increase in filtered and low tar cigarette sales from the 1950s through the 1980s resulted from consumers'' belief that these products were less harmful, as a result of Defendants'' extensive marketing of these products:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'regarding-perceived-health-benefits-menthol', '972', 'Regarding the perceived health benefits of menthol cigarettes, the compilation stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '660942115-2116-2115-us-53580-emphasis', '973', '660942115-2116 at 2115 (US 53580) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'wells-gave-his-views-b', '973', 'Wells gave his views that B&W should respond to attacks on low delivery cigarettes in the following manner:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '680592164-2169-2164-2168-us-21009-no', '973', '680592164-2169 at 2164-2168 (US 21009); (no bates) (US 76213); Wells WD, 46:11-49:3.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'marketed-filtered-low-tar-cigarettes', '974', 'marketed filtered or low tar cigarettes as less harmful than regular cigarettes." Similarly, Sharon Smith, former Director of Marketing Services and Operations at B&W, denied that the words "low tar" communicates any health benefit, stating that "I would not say that low tar implies any sort of benefit, other than it''s lower in tar." Ivey WD, 51:9-13; Smith WD, 66:19-22.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'may-2004-b-w-stated', '976', 'May 2004, B&W stated on its website that brand descriptors were intended only to communicate taste:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'tlt1040056-0062-0061-us-88628-ivey', '976', 'TLT1040056-0062 at 0061 (US 88628); Ivey WD, 70:5-14.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'd-batco', '976', 'd. BATCo'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '1-batco-s-research-low', '976', '(1) BATCo''s Research on the Low Tar Cigarette Category'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '100427791-7800-7794-us-34641-emphasis', '977', '100427791-7800 at 7794 (US 34641) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'addition-being-profitable-future-projections', '979', '. . . In addition to being profitable, future projections indicate an even faster growth of lights." Ivey'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'wd-76-10-12-ivey-wd', '979', 'WD, 76:10-12. Ivey WD, 82:4-11, 76:10-18; 321683062-3099 at 3087, 3090, 3065 (US 28586).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'check-concept-evaluation-stated-under', '979', 'Check & Concept Evaluation," stated, under the heading "Attitudes to LTN [low tar and nicotine]":'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '800056515-6581-6526-us-31643', '979', '800056515-6581 at 6526 (US 31643).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '700767443-7457-7452-us-22123-accord', '979', '700767443-7457 at 7452 (US 22123); accord 321184656-4672 (US 22045).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'accelerate-its-lights-segment-growth', '979', '"accelerate its lights segment growth." Under the heading of "Key Insights from 1997," the plan reported that "[l]ights franchise is skewed towards upscale 35+ female smokers, this is consistent with associated smoker (who is assumed to be health conscious)" and that "''[h]ealth conscious'' brand choice is seen by ASU [adult smokers under] 30s as a purchase pattern for 40+ smokers." 321551304-1323 at 1304, 1305 (US 22057); Ivey WD, 78:1-13.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'conclusions-section-stated-light-brands', '980', 'The "Conclusions" Section stated: "Light brands are primarily perceived as . . . less harmful for one''s health (easier breathing, better physical state in general). . . . Some of the females perceive the concept of ULTRA LIGHTS as . . . the last step before giving up smoking," and noted that 18-24 year olds "ranked health care features of lights most highly." 760008596-8803 at 8686, 8692-8693 (US 54588) (Confidential).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', '321628040-8076-8056-8059-8061-us', '981', '321628040-8076 at 8056, 8059, 8061 (US 22060).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'descriptors-not-intended-make-any', '981', 'descriptors was "not intended to make any health claims," and was "not meant to imply that light or ultra-light cigarettes are less harmful." Ivey WD, 71:20-72:3.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'until-acquired-b-w-1995', '982', 'until they were acquired by B&W in 1995. Gesell PD, State of Minnesota v. Philip Morris Inc., 9/18/97, 6:10-17; 117:3-15; 25:23-26:3; 93:2-13. Like the other Defendants, American Tobacco used descriptive terms and low FTC tar ratings to convey misleading and unsubstantiated health messages to the public regarding their low tar cigarettes.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'atx040070514-0519-0514-us-21125-see', '982', 'ATX040070514-0519 at 0514(US 21125); see also ADV011 1575-1579 (US 3028); ADV107 0020- 0022 (US 88689); ADV107 0023-0027 (US 88690) (1964 Carlton advertisements).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'developed-appeal-those-smokers-preferring', '983', '"was developed to appeal to those smokers preferring a light cigarette -- one that is low in ''tar'' -- and nicotine yield," achieved "sizeable sales increases in 1967" resulting from "favorable publicity" as a low tar, low nicotine cigarette. MNAT00029170-9201 at 9176 (US 21222).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'PEOPLE WHO SMOKE FILTER CIGARETTES . . . ARE MORE CONSCIOUSLY IN CONFLICT ABOUT SMOKING . . . . THEY CAN''T COMPLETELY ENJOY SMOKING BECAUSE THEY KNOW IT IS NOT HEALTHY. . . . THEY MAY BE RECEPTIVE TO ADVERTISING WHICH HELPS THEM ESCAPE FROM', 'tar-u-s-government-testing', '983', '''tar'' by U.S. Government testing and cited its "unique Air-Stream Filter" as the source of its ability to reduce tar to 4 mg. (as compared to what was then the industry average of over 20 mg.).'),
