('us-v-philip-morris', 'The Defendants Need Youth as Replacement Smokers', 'opportunities-martin-orlowsky-ceo-lorillard', '1006', 'Opportunities," to Martin Orlowsky, CEO of Lorillard, Diane Burrows, market researcher at R.J. Reynolds, stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'The Defendants Need Youth as Replacement Smokers', '503049069-9072-9069-us-20711-501431517-1610', '1006', '503049069-9072 at 9069 (US 20711); 501431517-1610 at 1519 (US 20680); 506653291-3348 at'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'The Defendants Need Youth as Replacement Smokers', '3291-3296-us-85235', '1006', '3291, 3296 (US 85235).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'The Defendants Need Youth as Replacement Smokers', 'implications-90-s-are-eighteen', '1008', '"Implications for 90''s" are that eighteen to twenty-four year olds will be "[c]ritical to long term brand vitality as consumption increases with age." Another report prepared for RJR, from approximately 1989, titled "Younger Adult Smokers," discussed the strategic importance of younger adult smokers, stating that "YAS are the only source of replacement smokers-[l]ess than one-third of smokers start after age 18." The report analyzed the differences between "FUBYAS" [First Brand Young Adult Smokers] (ages 18 to 20) and "Switchers" (ages 21 to 24), stating that "FUBYAS are in transition -- belonging to the FAMILY (secure) replaced by belonging to selected PEER GROUP (not as secure)." MBDOJ06953-6966 at 6955-6956, 6969, 6993, 6996 (US 59747) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'The Defendants Need Youth as Replacement Smokers', '507181261-1261-us-20007-emphasis-original', '1008', '507181261-1261 (US 20007) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'The Defendants Need Youth as Replacement Smokers', '513869196-9303-9197-9198-us-30058', '1009', '513869196-9303 at 9197, 9198 (US 30058) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'The Defendants Need Youth as Replacement Smokers', 'schoenbachler-pd-united-states-v', '1009', 'Schoenbachler PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 5/21/02, 72:16-21, 73:13-22, 141:11-141:21,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'play-key-role-process-recruiting', '1010', 'play a key role in the process of recruiting young, new smokers by exposing young people to massive amounts of imagery associating positive qualities with cigarette smoking. Research in psychology and cognitive neuroscience demonstrates how powerful such imagery can be, particularly for young people, in suppressing perception of risk and encouraging behavior. Slovic WD, 53:22-63:11 Defendants'' own statistics demonstrate how successful they have been in marketing their three main youth brands: Philip Morris''s Marlboro, RJR''s Camel, and Lorillard''s Newport.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'no-bates-je-063621-516-17', '1010', '(no bates) (JE 063621 at 516-17) (1989 Surgeon General Report).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'vxa1601844-2232-1874-us-64057-government', '1011', 'VXA1601844-2232 at 1874 (US 64057). Government expert Dr. Dean Krugman noted he would'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'never-phrase-question-relationship-between', '1011', '"never phrase the question [of the relationship between marketing and youth smoking initiation] in a causal manner":'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'krugman-tt-12-16-04', '1011', 'Krugman TT, 12/16/04, 8901:2-4, 8915:10-18; see also Krugman WD, 158:18-159:4 ("the advertising/promotion and smoking initiation/continuation relationship is not an empirically verifiable phenomenon"). For more on Dr. Krugman''s credentials, see 2681, infra.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'uxa013058-0484-0362-us-64693', '1012', 'UXA013058-0484 at 0362 (US 64693).'),
