('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'research-division-publication-effect-tobacco', '1014', 'Research Division publication, "The Effect of Tobacco Advertising on Tobacco Consumption: A'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'discussion-document-reviewing-evidence-concluded', '1014', 'Discussion Document Reviewing the Evidence," concluded that:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', '0212977-3036-0243-us-34282-department', '1014', '0212977-3036 at 0243 (US 34282). The Department of Health further concluded, regarding studies of advertising bans in other countries, that "[i]n each case the banning of advertising was followed by a fall in smoking on a scale which cannot reasonably be attributed to other factors [other than the advertising ban]." Id.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'hha2242048-2211-2122-us-33038', '1015', 'HHA2242048-2211 at 2122 (US 33038).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'general-nci-s-monograph-14', '1015', 'General. NCI''s Monograph 14: Changing Adolescent Smoking Prevalence, a 2001 National Cancer'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'institute-publication-found', '1015', 'Institute publication, found:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'cxa0240054-0325-0079-us-72977', '1015', 'CXA0240054-0325 at 0079 (US 72977).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'marketing-youth-smoking-longitudinal-studies', '1016', 'marketing and youth smoking. "Longitudinal studies, which collect data at two or more points in time, can help sort out the ''directionality'' of the relationship between advertising and smoking behavior." Eriksen (Liability) WD, 75:15-17; see also Biglan TT, 1/11/05, 9638:11-20; Eriksen TT, 1/27/05, 11471:12-11472:22.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'eriksen-liability-wd-76-16-78', '1017', 'Eriksen (Liability) WD, 76:16-78:22; (no bates) (US 17684).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'evidence-including-survey-data-scientific', '1019', 'evidence, including survey data, scientific studies and experiments, and behavioral and econometric studies, supports the conclusion that cigarette marketing is a substantial contributing factor in the smoking behavior of young people, including the decision to begin smoking and the decision to continue smoking. Eriksen (Liability) WD, 1:20-3:19.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'biglan-wd-37-1-10-central', '1022', 'Biglan WD, 37: 1-10. The central purpose of the tobacco companies'' image advertising is motivating adolescents to smoke.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'id-95-23-96-5', '1022', 'Id. at 95:23-96:5.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'relations-university-georgia-has-published', '1022', 'Relations at the University of Georgia, has published over thirty peer-reviewed articles on marketing, particularly tobacco marketing, including an article, titled "Teenage Exposure to Cigarette'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'advertising-popular-consumer-magazines-published', '1022', 'Advertising in Popular Consumer Magazines," published in 2000. Dr. Krugman has also served as a reviewer for numerous scholarly journals, including the Journal of Broadcasting & Electronic'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'media-journal-marketing-research-currently', '1022', 'Media, and the Journal of Marketing Research, and is currently a Member of the Editorial Board of the Journal of Advertising.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'id-84-25-85-8', '1023', 'Id. at 84:25-85:8.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'id-160-8-12', '1023', 'Id. at 160:8-12.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'center-disease-control-prevention-s', '1023', 'Center for Disease Control and Prevention''s Office of Smoking and Health ("OSH"), the primary federal agency responsible for coordinating tobacco and health issues. From 1992 to 2000 at OSH,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'dr-eriksen-responsible-preparation-reports', '1023', 'Dr. Eriksen was responsible for the preparation of the Reports of the Surgeon General. In addition,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'dr-eriksen-has-researched-published', '1023', 'Dr. Eriksen has researched and published about the tobacco industry and tobacco-related disease control and prevention for over twenty years. Dr. Eriksen has written nearly eighty peer-reviewed articles and books on tobacco-related issues and has received numerous professional awards and honors.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'defendants-cigarette-marketing-substantial-contributing', '1024', 'Defendants'' cigarette marketing is a substantial contributing factor to youth smoking initiation and continuation. Eriksen (Liability) WD, 55:4-8. Dr. Eriksen also concluded that adolescent smoking initiation is an immature behavior, one driven by the psychosocial development of adolescents and the cigarette brand imagery that corresponds precisely to adolescent aspirations. Eriksen (Liability)'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'wd-3-14-16', '1024', 'WD, 3:14-16.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'one-cause-among-many-eriksen', '1024', '"one cause among many." Eriksen TT, 2/02/05, 11892:7-15, 11893:18-25, 11894:3-19. He provided extensive and clear testimony on this point:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'a-yes', '1024', 'A. Yes.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'eriksen-tt-2-02-05', '1025', 'Eriksen TT, 2/02/05, 11892:7-15, 11893:18-25, 11894:3-19.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'biglan-tt-1-11-05', '1025', 'Biglan TT, 1/11/05, 9681:3-8.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'defendants-finally-many-their-conclusions', '1026', 'Defendants. Finally, many of their conclusions were consistent, even though they each drew from different studies and segments of the field.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'no-bates-jd-004744-ch', '1028', '(no bates) (JD 004744 at ch. 2, 2-5).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'cigarette-brand-names-logos-advertising', '1029', 'Cigarette brand names, logos, and advertising messages are pervasive. (no bates) (US 64831) (1998 Surgeon General Report at 220). While cigarette industry advertising and sales promotion strategies have changed quickly over the years in response to different types of regulation, cigarette products still maintain a very high profile in terms of images and messages reaching teenagers. By making their cigarette products and messages ubiquitous, the tobacco companies normalize smoking and make smoking an acceptable behavior among adolescents. Tobacco companies'' plans indicate their intent to make their brands an ever-present part of the culture, "while becoming a fabric of the community." 2041940822-0852 at 0822 (US 38244).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'publish-research-area-recently-published', '1030', 'publish research in this area and recently published a book, titled "Smoking: Risk, Perception, and Policy." He has been a Professor in the Department of Psychology at the University of Oregon since 1986, and the President of Decision Research in Eugene, Oregon. Dr. Slovic is a charter fellow of the American Psychological Society and a fellow of the American Psychological Association. In addition, he currently serves on the editorial boards of Risk Analysis, Risk Abstracts, Behavioral Decision Making, Risk, Decision and Policy, and the Journal of Psychology and Financial Markets.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'has-written-over-300-peer-reviewed', '1032', 'He has written over 300 peer-reviewed articles and almost fifty book chapters on subjects related to the pharmacology of nicotine and nicotine addiction. He was also a senior scientific editor and contributing author of the 1988 Report of the Surgeon General. Dr. Benowitz also served as a peer reviewer for the Surgeon General''s 1994 Report concerning tobacco use by youth. Based on his academic credentials, his clinical experience as an attending and consulting physician, his work for the Surgeon General, and his prodigious output of peer-reviewed articles, the Court credits his testimony. According to Dr. Benowitz:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'benowitz-wd-40-8-11-vxa0130158-0484', '1032', 'Benowitz WD, 40:8-11; VXA0130158-0484 at 0256-0260 (US 64693) (1994 Surgeon General Report, Tables 20 and 22).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'slovic-wd-20-16-21-5', '1033', 'Slovic WD, 20:16-21:5. Surveys have demonstrated that individuals have little knowledge of the reality of the pain, suffering, and despair of those with lung cancer, emphysema, congestive heart failure, and other smoking related diseases. One survey showed that 53% of adolescent smokers and 49% of adult smokers know "a little" or "not much at all" about the pain and suffering associated with lung cancer. Likewise, 68% of adolescent smokers and 54% of adult smokers know "a little" or "not much at all" about the pain and suffering associated with emphysema. More than 70% of adults and 80% of adolescents overestimated the likelihood that lung cancer is curable. Slovic WD, 19:4-20:15 (citing Weinstein, N.D., Slovic, P., Waters, E., and Gibson, G., Public Understanding of the Illnesses Caused by Cigarette Smoking, Nicotine and Tobacco Research (April 2004)).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Is a Substantial Contributing Factor to Youth', 'almost-one-third-seniors-who', '1036', 'Almost one third of seniors who smoked a pack a day thought that they, too, would quit within five years. Only 13% actually quit. Weinstein WD, 66:3-69:19.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'under-twenty-one-especially-those-under', '1036', 'under twenty-one, and especially those under eighteen. Defendants want to draw a bright line between tracking and targeting youth. Defendants claim that tracking is only a research tool to obtain information about youth and that targeting is the directing of all forms of marketing at a particular demographic group, i.e., people under the age of twenty-one. Whether all of the activity detailed below is labeled tracking or targeting is simply a matter of semantics. The activities have the same purpose: to start young people smoking and to keep them smoking. Defendants'' argument that their tracking was not done to determine youth preferences and behaviors so as to market to youth more effectively, is patently not credible. Despite their denials that they used such information for marketing purposes, the evidence indicates that Defendants tracked youth in order to determine how best to induce them to start, and continue, smoking cigarettes.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2022239142-9147-9142-9144-us-22931', '1037', '2022239142-9147 at 9142, 9144 (US 22931).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2026234664-4669-4664-4665-4667-us-20424', '1039', '2026234664-4669 at 4664, 4665-4667 (US 20424). Since 1968, Marlboro''s share of the youngest demographic group has always been substantially higher than Marlboro''s overall market share. Morgan PT, Minnesota v. Philip Morris, 4/24/98, 13907:12-19.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1002375102-5107-5102-us-20135', '1039', '1002375102-5107 at 5102 (US 20135).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'holbert-philip-morris-marketing-research', '1040', 'Holbert, Philip Morris Marketing Research Department, to numerous Philip Morris employees, discussed findings from a survey conducted by the Opinion Research Corporation of smoking incidence among 452 twelve to seventeen year olds and those age eighteen and older. The survey found that 13% of the twelve to seventeen year olds polled smoked at least a pack a week.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2041761791-1801-1791-1795-us-21493', '1040', '2041761791-1801 at 1791, 1795 (US 21493).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1005159031-9168-9034-9043-9044-us-26207', '1040', '1005159031-9168 at 9034, 9043-9044 (US 26207).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'competition-marlboro-s-franchise-smokers', '1040', 'Competition for Marlboro''s Franchise Smokers" stated, "for the past year, Marlboro''s growth in share of market has slowed down considerably. . . . [T]his problem is especially clear among the most important segment of the Marlboro franchise, smokers aged 18 to 24." In response to this trend, the memorandum reported that the "Roper Organization was commissioned to undertake [a] study . . . with the intention of probing the dynamics of the market among smokers below the age of 24. (This was not the ''usual'' sample of age 18-24; in this study, no lower age limit was set.)" Roper conducted 1050 interviews for this study. Comparing Roper''s results and Philip Morris''s own National Tracking Study, the document reported that the results were not significantly different, but "[t]he somewhat larger share for Marlboro smokers found in the Roper Study (33% Vs. 27% found in Tracking) may be accounted for by the popularity of this brand among those under age eighteen who are not interviewed in Tracking," but who were interviewed by Roper. The Roper Study determined that "Marlboro is still the most frequent ''first regular brand''" and stated, "[t]he ideal situation would be to have lots of people choosing our brand as their first (which we do)." According to the Roper Study:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2022245802-5823-5803-5804-5807-5808', '1041', '2022245802-5823 at 5803, 5804, 5807, 5808, 5809 (US 26748).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1002646151-6185-6152-6154-6157-us-20140', '1042', '1002646151-6185 at 6152, 6154-6157 (US 20140).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1975-1980-written-myron-e-johnston', '1042', '1975-1980," written by Myron E. Johnston, Senior Economist for Research and Development, stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'johnston-also-predicted-because-declining', '1042', 'Johnston also predicted that, because of the declining number of fifteen to nineteen year olds:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1000739883-9907-9903-9905-9907-us', '1042', '1000739883-9907 at 9903, 9905, 9907 (US 21601).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'marlboro-red-growth-slowdown-slower', '1042', 'Marlboro Red growth slowdown: slower growth in the number of fifteen to nineteen year olds, the recession, increasing cigarette prices, and the "changing brand preferences of younger smokers."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'johnston-stated', '1042', 'Johnston stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1003285497-5502-5497-us-20160', '1043', '1003285497-5502 at 5497 (US 20160).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2024921314-1612-1374-us-20403', '1043', '2024921314-1612 at 1374 (US 20403).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'most-smokers-appear-have-begun', '1044', '"most smokers appear to have begun smoking between the ages of 10 and 18." The memorandum identified the "factors involved in the initiation of smoking," explaining:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'respect-high-school-students-memorandum', '1044', 'With respect to high school students, the memorandum stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'udow-indicated-consulted-both-external', '1044', 'Udow indicated that he consulted both external, independent research and internal Philip Morris research on youth smoking: "Information on the motivation that leads to a continuation of smoking comes from a special study done for Philip Morris (Brand, 1971)." 1000744089-4096 at 4089, 4092, 4095-4096 (US 20106).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-indicated-philip-morris-s', '1045', 'The report indicated Philip Morris''s concern over demographic and social trends that were creating a downturn in teenage smoking rate: "Because of our high share of the market among the youngest smokers, Philip Morris will suffer more than other companies from the decline in the number of teenage smokers." 1000390803-0855 at 0808-0809 (US 22334).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1003478157-8159-8157-us-35772-emphasis', '1046', '1003478157-8159 at 8157 (US 35772) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2028817401-7576-7504-us-20016', '1046', '2028817401-7576 at 7504 (US 20016).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'johnston-further-stated', '1047', 'Johnston further stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2040280951-0977-0954-0955-us-37496', '1047', '2040280951-0977 at 0954-0955 (US 37496).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'kool-newport-new-smokers-entering', '1047', 'Kool, and Newport: "New smokers entering the market were disproportionately attracted to those brands." The report stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-further-stated-2', '1047', 'The report further stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2001265000-5045-5012-5030-us-20299', '1048', '2001265000-5045 at 5012, 5030 (US 20299).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2040282066-2092-2066-us-20437', '1048', '2040282066-2092 at 2066 (US 20437).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2045287048-7092-7061-7063-7064-us', '1048', '2045287048-7092 at 7061, 7063, 7064 (US 38407).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'vice-president-philip-morris-summarized', '1048', 'Vice President at Philip Morris, summarized "Key Marlboro Issues." According to Brennan:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'order-maximize-share-marlboro-should', '1049', 'In order to maximize share, Marlboro should'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2045305938-5942-5938-5939-5941-us', '1049', '2045305938-5942 at 5938, 5939, 5941 (US 26948).');
INSERT INTO passages (report, section, paragraph_id, page, body) VALUES
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'marketing-philip-morris-provided-details', '1050', 'Marketing at Philip Morris, provided "details regarding the upcoming Camel qualitative study" and stated that "[r]ecent strong Camel performance, especially among the young male target, has resulted in an effort to explain that success and determine the potential threat to Marlboro." The letter indicated that respondents for this study were to be "recruited among 18-24 year old smokers." 2045471014-1015 at 1014 (US 20461).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2026230097-0713-0211-us-20423', '1050', '2026230097-0713 at 0211 (US 20423).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2046569728-9731-9728-9729-9730-us-20471', '1051', '2046569728-9731 at 9728, 9729-9730 (US 20471).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2071032180-2206-2181-2185-2187-us', '1052', '2071032180-2206 at 2181, 2185, 2187 (US 21964).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1603-us-20395', '1052', '1603 (US 20395).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2044895379-5484-5389-us-85185', '1052', '2044895379-5484 at 5389 (US 85185).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'questions-asked-include-promotions-may', '1053', 'Questions asked include: the promotions they may have seen or purchased; the cigarette brands they have purchased in the last week; the type of store at which they purchase cigarettes; whether they are saving Marlboro Miles; their knowledge of certain brand images; promotion and advertising awareness; and the number and ages of all smokers in the household. Levy PD, California v. Philip Morris, 6/23/98, 18:18-30:12; Levy WD, 17:18-20:15, 27:2-28:19, 41:7-43:18, 48:4-51:21.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2-philip-morris-examined-lifestyles', '1054', '(2) Philip Morris examined the lifestyles and attitudes of eighteen to twenty-four year old male smokers to explain their brand choices, including their leisure time activities (e.g., hanging out with friends, keeping car looking good, talking on the phone with friends, going to bars or rock concerts), social circles, attitudes about smoking, brand image, and their aspirations and objectives; (3) Philip Morris profiled male Marlboro smokers between the ages of eighteen and twenty-four and compared them with the profiles of Camel male smokers of the same age; (4) Philip Morris determined that the Marlboro Brand image among eighteen to twenty-four year old males included: cool, outgoing, popular, outdoorsy, adventurous, and independent; (5) Philip Morris''s profile of an eighteen to twenty-four year old male Marlboro smoker was a relaxed smoker who feels unpressured; (6) Philip Morris determined that, unlike Marlboro smokers, Camel smokers were attracted by the individuality of their brand (and the advertising packaging); (7) Philip Morris researched the size of its smoker base and determined that Marlboro male smokers age eighteen to twenty-four made a disproportionately high contribution to Marlboro''s total volume comprising seven million smokers, and accounting for one in five of Philip Morris''s total smokers; and (8) Philip Morris determined that smokers eighteen to nineteen shared a similar racial make-up and that 86% were white males who smoked Marlboro Red. 2048735500-5604 at 5501, 5505, 5508, 5518, 5531-5541, 5543, 5547, 5555 (US 21971).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'conclusion-corresponding-table-omitted-from', '1055', 'This conclusion and the corresponding table were omitted from the final version of the memorandum and attachment, which were sent on December 9, 1994. 2046828693-8693 (US 21802);'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2046828694-8697-us-21803-2046828612-8615-8612', '1055', '2046828694-8697 (US 21803); 2046828612-8615 at 8612 (US 20479) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'historically-low-appeared-be-stabilizing', '1055', '. . . historically low, appeared to be stabilizing at about 14%." The analysis also concluded:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2040171445-1455-1445-1446-us-37478', '1055', '2040171445-1455 at 1445, 1446 (US 37478*).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'under-heading-notes-from-editor', '1056', 'Under the heading "Notes from the Editor," Franklin, listed as Editor-In-Chief, explained the purpose of the project:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'half-study-s-participants-non-smokers', '1056', 'Half of the study''s participants were non-smokers. 2041601887-1931 at 1888, 1889, 1891 (US 38213); Norris PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 7/31/03, 238:25-250:6.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'levan-pd-united-states-v', '1057', 'LeVan PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/25/02 148:12-18; see also 2063684338-4340 (US 39817).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1-10-05-levan-regard', '1058', '1/10/05 (LeVan). With regard to the "College Scan" document, LeVan agreed with the statement:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'marlboro-scores-far-away-highest', '1058', '"Marlboro scores by far and away the highest in terms of brand usage and smoking incidence . . ."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'among-eighteen-year-olds-levan', '1058', 'among eighteen year olds. LeVan PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/25/02, 185:19-22.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'us-38434', '1058', '(US 38434).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'generation-examination-generation-x-discussed', '1058', 'Generation:'' An Examination of Generation X," discussed the Roper organization''s study of the purchasing behavior of Generation X, those born between 1966 and 1985, i.e., eleven to thirty year olds. The analysis was prepared for Philip Morris and presented to a group of Philip Morris Brand and Consumer Research employees. 2047130104-0170 (US 38583).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'additionally-document-noted-p-oint', '1059', 'Additionally, the document noted that "[p]oint of purchase is the key source of brand visibility."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'lb0170038-0053-0038-0042-0044-0050', '1060', 'LB0170038-0053 at 0038, 0042, 0044, 0050 (US 25906).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'director-market-research-lorillard-discussed', '1061', 'Director of Market Research at Lorillard, discussed a Lorillard study which sampled the smoking behavior of students as young as sixteen years of age. 89834681-4684 at 4681 (US 21108).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '81560431-0496-0438-us-85200-first', '1062', '81560431-0496 at 0438 (US 85200). In the first volume of Eastman''s 1969 study of cigarette smoking behavior and attitudes, Eastman looked closely at smoking initiation behavior of individuals ages seven to twenty-one. Eastman found that over thirty percent of young males obtained their first cigarette, not from parents, friends or relatives, but from buying it (over 10%), stealing it (over 15%), or making it (nearly 10%). Both boys and girls reported about equally that their first cigarette made them feel grown-up. Among the subset of interviewees sixteen to twenty-four years of age, nearly 20% of males and over 10% of females reported feeling "big," while nearly 20% of both sexes mentioned confidence and security as reasons why they started smoking. The study also examined regular smoking among youth ages thirteen and up. Id. at 0454-0455, 0458, 0460, 0465-0471. The second volume of Eastman''s 1969 study of cigarette smoking behavior and attitudes included a survey of the literature published between 1967 and 1969 on the smoking behavior of children as young as eleven, as well as teenagers. 81560497-0541 at 0500-0508 (US 85201).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'lorillard-president-curtis-h-judge', '1063', 'Lorillard President Curtis H. Judge, regarding Lorillard''s analysis of its own and its competitors'' brand shares by age. Satterthwaite stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '91270029-0030-0029-us-21109', '1063', '91270029-0030 at 0029 (US 21109).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1974-1975-gallup-gauged-effectiveness-advertising', '1063', '1974-1975," by Gallup gauged the effectiveness of advertising in particular magazines, including in the category of "Glamour (Age 15-34)" magazines such as, among others, Seventeen and Teen.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '03496228-6630-us-20057', '1063', '03496228-6630 (US 20057).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'menthol-from-r-e-ritchie', '1063', 'Menthol," from R.E. Ritchie to A.J. Bass at Lorillard reported that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '91529112-9114-9112-us-21110', '1063', '91529112-9114 at 9112 (US 21110).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '03537131-32-us-22357', '1065', '03537131-32 (US 22357).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '01110991-0992-je-021604-attached-document', '1065', '01110991-0992 (JE 021604), attached a document, titled "Replies to 5-year Plan Questionnaire," which stated that "the easiest [brand] to keep riding is Newport. However, I think we must continually keep in mind that Newport is being heavily supported by blacks and the under 18 smokers. We are on somewhat thin ice should either of these two groups decide to shift their smoking habits." 01110993-1032 at 1030 (US 20031).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'dickinson-research-titled-exploratory-study', '1065', 'Dickinson Research, titled "An Exploratory Study for Newport Smoking and Purchase Behavior of'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'young-adults-stated', '1065', 'Young Adults," stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-further-stated-both-male', '1065', 'The report further stated: "Both the male and female respondents thought of the typical Newport smoker as ''young,'' and both cited Newport as a brand used by those who are just starting to smoke."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '84411662-1689-1669-1680-us-55999', '1065', '84411662-1689 at 1669,1680 (US 55999); 83896981-7009 at 6989, 7000 (US 55927).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'chemist-m-sudholt-manager-analytical', '1066', 'Chemist, to M.A. Sudholt, Manager of Analytical Development, on the subject of "Idea Session July'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '27-1982-tobacco-science-group', '1066', '27, 1982 of the Tobacco Science Group" contained a proposal that "Video Game Imagery [be] incorporated in pack design (youth appeal)." It detailed:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '96509517-9519-9519-us-56890', '1066', '96509517-9519 at 9519 (US 56890).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'september-2-1983-memorandum-curtis', '1066', 'September 2, 1983 memorandum to Curtis H. Judge, President of Lorillard, that "because the number of teenagers is declining rapidly, even a stable smoking incidence would mean a declining number of entering smokers." 03922854-2854 (US 21755).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '---young-menthol-smokers-provided', '1066', '-- Young Menthol Smokers" provided ways for an interviewer to gather information about young smokers. This document included a list of questions to ask young adults, including:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '85377724-7729-7725-7727-us-21078-march', '1067', '85377724-7729 at 7725-7727 (US 21078). In a March 8, 1984 memorandum, titled "Young Menthol Smoker Focus Groups," to S.T. Jones, Lorillard Director of Product Development and Marketing Research, Laurie Moroz discussed "observations and hypotheses" from these focus groups and stated: "the females in the 18 to 24 year old age group are more experimental and open to new brands than males." 85377682-7682 (US 87806); 85377680-7681 at 7680 (US 87807).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '92092650-2651-2650-us-57159', '1068', '92092650-2651 at 2650 (US 57159).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-also-stated-lorillard-s', '1069', 'This report also stated that "Lorillard''s Newport brand recognizes younger adult smokers as an important consumer base for this cigarette. This market is defined as a ''twenty-something'' market; adults ages 18-29." 91950191-0242 at 0193, 0195 (US 74423) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'department-karl-w-schullinger-assistant', '1069', 'Department to Karl W. Schullinger, Assistant to the Advertising Manager, stated that "the largest potential market for Lucky Strike is in the younger age groups," and that "Bonanza" would be a better television venue for Lucky Strike than "Lawrence Welk" because "Bonanza" was viewed by a greater number of people in the "younger age groups." An attached chart showed that three times as many "Teen-Agers (boys and girls 13-17)" watch "Bonanza" as watch "Lawrence Welk." ATX030308900-8901 at 8900 (US 20583).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '105408812-8815-8812-8813-us-26273', '1070', '105408812-8815 at 8812-8813 (US 26273).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'researchers-telephoned-approximately-4-500', '1071', 'The researchers telephoned approximately 4,500 individuals in the age groups of sixteen to twenty, twenty-one to thirty-four, thirty-five to forty-nine, and fifty and over. In addition, "Age and sex quotas were assigned so as to yield the correct proportions of teen-age contacts and adult male and female contacts." MNAT00405881-5912 at 5883-5585 (US 88157).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '680135996-6002-5996-5997-5998-us-20989', '1072', '680135996-6002 at 5996-5997, 5998 (US 20989). Johnson explained the reason for its targeted approach:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'id-emphasis-original', '1072', 'Id. (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'study-concluded-younger-smoker-pre-eminent', '1073', 'The study concluded that "the younger smoker is of pre-eminent importance." 779217759-7833 at'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '7760-7763-7768-7827-us-21054', '1073', '7760, 7763-7768, 7827 (US 21054); 779217758-7793 at 7760, 7768 (US 85211).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'l-johnson-b-w-s', '1073', 'L. Johnson in B&W''s Advertising and Marketing Planning Department (which he subsequently managed), stressed the importance of effective marketing to young "starters" for the continued profitability of the company. The plan stated that, although B&W''s share of smokers under twentyfive was greater than the rest of the industry, this was due entirely to Kool: "[w]ithout Kool''s influence, the Company''s profile is female, old and getting older . . . a relatively undesirable situation." The document anticipated a coming battle over the shrinking pool of sixteen to twentyfive year old potential smokers:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'plan-indicated-youth-smokers-market', '1073', 'The plan indicated that youth smokers were the market''s growth: "among under 25 year olds, users have almost doubled. Kool''s growth in this market is the greatest of any brand. It is also the fastest growing cigarette in the total market." The plan recommended that "[n]ew ways to selectively reach younger smokers and females entering the market should be found. . . ." 682823798-3801 at 3801 (US 21032); 680500903-1076 at 0918, 0930, 0942, 0945 (US 21607).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '027887-7887-us-34185-smith-tt', '1074', '027887-7887 (US 34185); Smith TT, 1/7/05, 9247:1-9248:7.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'recruiting-qualifications-study-respondents-aged', '1076', 'The "recruiting qualifications" for the study were respondents "aged 16 or 17, attending high school, and smokers of 5 cigarettes or more per day." 566627826-7935 at 7839, 7840 (US 20939).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'strategies-achieve-objective-included-advertising', '1076', 'Strategies to achieve this objective included "advertising pressure against high filtration styles in young adult skewed publications" and to "[d]ominate specific young adult publications with a particular style." 680559149-9162 at 9149, 9152-9154 (US 54048).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '660110384-0386-us-20954', '1077', '660110384-0386 (US 20954).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-menthols-also-tracked-kool', '1077', 'The report on menthols also tracked Kool''s share of smokers ages sixteen to twenty-five and specifically noted Kool''s share of black male smokers ages sixteen to thirty-four. 670624932-5364 at 4932, 5008-5009, 5013-5014 (US 53869).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1980s-b-w-conducted-marketing', '1077', '1980s, B&W conducted marketing research on individuals as young as sixteen, specifically on the switching behaviors of individuals between the age of sixteen and twenty-five. Brookes PD, United'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'states-v-philip-morris-5', '1077', 'States v. Philip Morris, 5/2/02, 134:24-136:23, 146:18-147:18, 148:2-148:19.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'document-also-stated-kool-must', '1080', 'This document also stated that "Kool must aggressively seek to re-establish itself among young adults with aggressive programs" such as music events and outdoor advertising. 554000052-0060 at 0053 (US 20937).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '500287512-7596-7532-us-20624', '1081', '500287512-7596 at 7532 (US 20624).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'macgovern-william-esty-company-study', '1084', 'MacGovern of the William Esty Company to study high school students'' attitudes toward cigarette smoking. 501113763-3764 (US 22361). One of the conclusions reached in that study was that, "[p]reference-wise, CAMEL and WINSTON are shown as holding their shares substantially constant while SALEM increased its share, especially among high school students." 501113723-3730 at 3723 (US 22366).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '501795141-5141-us-20687', '1085', '501795141-5141 (US 20687).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'mid-1970s-rjr-became-aware-using', '1086', 'In the mid-1970s, RJR became aware by using various consumer research methods that their "share of market among younger people [was] much lower than it had to be in order to maximize [their] volume." Tredennick PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 5/13/02, 42:16-46:20, 104:3-105:05, 148:22-149:09, 144:05-22, 171:07-24. The data on "teenage smokers" (fourteen to seventeen) from the NFO included: the relative share of RJR in capturing this market; the share of each of the company''s competitors in this age group; RJR''s share among this age group among its own key brands; the share of the company''s competitors in this age group by key cigarette brands, the share of the total market broken down by age and gender, and the number of cigarettes smoked per day in this age group broken down by gender. 501443912-3921 at 3913-3915 (US 20681).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '500915683-5691-5686-5687-us-20659-teague', '1087', '500915683-5691 at 5686-5687 (US 20659). Teague repeated these statements, almost verbatim, in a 1973 memorandum discussing "factors influencing pre-smokers to try smoking, learn to smoke and become confirmed smokers." 502987407-7418 at 7408 (US 20708).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '502987407-502987418-7408-us-20708', '1088', '502987407-502987418 at 7408 (US 20708).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'watson-rjr-concerning-national-family', '1088', 'Watson at RJR concerning National Family Opinion preference share data for fourteen to twenty year old Marlboro and Winston smokers. McCain wrote that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '508453918-3920-3919-us-20812', '1088', '508453918-3920 at 3919 (US 20812).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'expose-management-opportunity-aggressively-position', '1088', '"to expose Management to the opportunity to aggressively position Camel Filter against the young adult market (male)." The proposal stated that males aged fourteen to thirty-four "represent approximately 35% of 85 mm [length] NFF [non-filter full flavor] smokers." 500723696-3718 at'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '501166152-6153-us-23051', '1089', '501166152-6153 (US 23051).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'table-titled-age-started-smoking', '1090', 'A table titled "Age Started Smoking," which included a category for "12 & Under," was appended to this memorandum. 501899346-9359 at 9346, 9351, 9352 (US 20688).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'presentation-discussed-importance-youth-smokers', '1090', 'The presentation discussed the importance of youth smokers in reestablishing RJR''s share of market growth and setting the marketing strategy that would be implemented to gain market share among youth. 500746950-6976 at 6951 (US 21609). A November 26, 1974 memorandum, titled "R.J. Reynolds Tobacco Company Domestic Operating Goals," stated: "Winston has 14% of this franchise, while Marlboro has 33% – Salem has 9% – Kool has 17%." The memorandum indicated that RJR "will direct advertising appeal to this young adult group without alienating the brand''s current franchise." 500796928-6934 at 6928 (US 22363); 500796976-6983 at 6977 (US 21610).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'handwritten-cover-memorandum-secret-hind', '1091', 'A handwritten cover memorandum to the "Secret" Hind memorandum revealed that Tucker subsequently obtained company approval of the "Turk" recommendation. 505775556-5561 at 5556, 5557 (US 78787).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '500769032-9036-9032-us-21814', '1092', '500769032-9036 at 9032 (US 21814).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'r-j-reynolds-tobacco-company', '1092', 'R.J. Reynolds Tobacco Company":'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'leary-pd-united-states-v', '1092', 'Leary PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 5/2/02,102:9-105:11; 501630269-0288 at 0283 (US'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '21605', '1092', '21605).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1976-memorandum-t-l-ogburn', '1092', '1976 memorandum to T.L. Ogburn, titled "Share of Smokers by Age Group," which contained "an annual update of trends." The memorandum stated that Winston King''s share among fourteen to seventeen year olds "is off two points for the second year in a row. Current share is 9%. Conversely,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'marlboro-king-s-share-among', '1093', 'Marlboro King''s share among this age group which had shown losses during the past three years was up one point. Current share is 32%." Key stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'under-corporate-comparisons-memorandum-stated', '1093', 'Under "Corporate Comparisons," the memorandum stated: "Philip Morris posted a 4 point gain among 14-17 year old smokers (RJR and B&W each lost 2 points)." 500234050-4051 (US 48071).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-further-predicted-reduction-number', '1093', 'The report further predicted a "reduction in the number of new smokers" due to "stronger enforcement of laws prohibiting sale of cigarettes to teen-agers," which, according to the report, would have a negative impact on RJR''s sales and profits. 500387795-7899 at 7822, 7836 (US 20631).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '94681077-1079-1077-1079-us-32322', '1094', '94681077-1079 at 1077, 1079 (US 32322); 501380878-0982 at 0878-0880 (US 48844).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'family-opinion-regarding-smoking-behavior', '1094', 'Family Opinion regarding the smoking behavior of fourteen to seventeen year old smokers.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '501443912-3921-us-20681-501098917-8922-us', '1094', '501443912-3921 (US 20681); 501098917-8922 (US 23050); 500768429-8438 (US 20649);'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '500768427-8428-us-22341-501254289-4301-us', '1094', '500768427-8428 (US 22341); 501254289-4301 (US 20674); 501254267-4283 (US 22342);'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '501757367-7384-us-22343-500768754-8754-us', '1094', '501757367-7384 (US 22343); 500768754-8754 (US 20650); 500794841-4843 (US 20653).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'department-employee-discussed-franchise-aging', '1095', 'Department employee, discussed "franchise aging" -- the process of young smokers entering the smoking population as older smokers leave the market, either because they quit or they die. The report stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-went-m-any-adult', '1095', 'The report went on: "[m]any adult smokers have already formed consistent smoking patterns by the time they enter the market at age 18." 501443912-3921 at 3912, 3915 (US 20681).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '500768427-8428-8427-us-22341', '1095', '500768427-8428 at 8427 (US 22341).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'b-w-s-share-among', '1096', 'B&W''s share among fourteen to seventeen year olds had declined. 500686301-6313 at 6302, 6303'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'memorandum-stated-rjr-continues-gradually', '1096', 'This memorandum stated that "RJR continues to gradually decline," and concluded, "[h]opefully, our various planned activities that will be implemented this fall will aid in some way in reducing or correcting these trends." 508453894-3894 (US 20811).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'executive-vice-president-marketing-sales', '1097', 'Executive Vice President of Marketing and Sales, titled "Younger Adult Smoker Opportunity'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'analysis----new-brands-l', '1097', 'Analysis -- New Brands," L.W. Hall stated about young smokers:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '501340949-0950-us-20677', '1097', '501340949-0950 (US 20677).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'agemix-system-included-age-breakdowns', '1097', 'AGEMIX system included age breakdowns of twelve to seventeen, eighteen to twenty-four, etc.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'burrows-stated-since-few-people', '1097', 'Burrows stated: "Since few people start smoking after age 24, we will assume that incidence remains fixed as a group ages past 24." 502661958-1963 (US 20704); 501291100-1101 (US 85234);'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'miller-attached-table-showing-priority', '1099', 'Miller attached a table showing "Priority Regions" and "Remaining Regions" by brand: Marlboro, Winston and Camel. This document was contained in a file titled "Youth Target." 505936377-6378 (US 50876).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 's-uccessful-repositioning-winston-requires', '1100', '"[s]uccessful repositioning [of Winston] requires young adult smokers." 700186251-6251 (US'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '700186256-6256-us-54465', '1100', '700186256-6256 (US 54465).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '518090228-0255-0233-0242-0244-0249-0251', '1101', '518090228-0255 at 0233, 0242, 0244-0249, 0251 (US 52152); 518090256-0268 at 0260-0265, 0267'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'research-tracking-data-accumulated-youth', '1101', 'of research and tracking data they accumulated on youth smoking initiation, tastes and preferences by employing themes which resonate with youth in their marketing campaigns. Krugman WD, 85:11-92:18. Defendants have focused their attention on young people under the age of twenty-one in order to recruit replacement smokers and have emphasized the popularity, physical attractiveness, and "coolness" of their youth brands. Above all, Defendants have burnished the image of their youth brands to convey rugged independence, rebelliousness, love of life, adventurousness, confidence, self-assurance, and belonging to the "in" crowd.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'advertising-campaign-advertisements-usually-depicted', '1102', 'advertising campaign. The advertisements usually depicted slim, independent, well-dressed attractive women smoking cigarettes. ADV0281229-1231 (US 10511); see also (no bates) (US 12983); (no bates) (US 12527); (no bates) (US 12453).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-further-stated-16-20', '1102', 'The report further stated: "The 16 to 20 year-old begins smoking for psychosocial reasons. The act of smoking is symbolic; it signifies adulthood, he smokes to enhance his image in the eyes of his peers." The document concluded: "As the force from the psycho-social symbolism subsides, the pharmacological effect takes over to sustain the habit, augmented by the secondary gratifications."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1000273741-3771-3749-us-26080-1003287880-7890', '1103', '1000273741-3771 at 3749 (US 26080); 1003287880-7890 (US 20163); 1003287836-7848 at 7836,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2001265000-5045-5030-us-20299', '1104', '2001265000-5045 at 5030 (US 20299).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2045287059-7067-7063-us-38408', '1104', '2045287059-7067 at 7063 (US 38408).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'regarding-threat-camel-document-stated', '1105', 'Regarding the threat of Camel, the document stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'meet-camel-s-threat-document', '1105', 'To meet Camel''s threat, the document discussed a potential new advertising campaign, in addition to the traditional Marlboro advertisements, which would be "designed to appeal specifically to the young, adult male; ads which are strong in subject and tonality thereby reinforcing our core position." 2025871433-1506 at 1434, 1438, 1440 (US 22054).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'morris-project-researching-consumers-thoughts', '1106', 'Morris project researching consumers'' thoughts about cigarettes. Levy''s notes stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2062145828-5833-5828-5833-us-85184', '1106', '2062145828-5833 at 5828, 5833 (US 85184). As Levy acknowledged, "Philip Morris knows that cigarettes are one of the things that adolescents use in their transition from childhood to adulthood," based both on this research and on published literature. Levy WD, 50:2-51:21.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'president-marketing-philip-morris-international', '1106', 'President of Marketing at Philip Morris International, explained how the race car drivers pictured in Marlboro advertisements represented a "contemporized" and "relevant" Marlboro man:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2045068451-8470-8456-8460-us-23931', '1106', '2045068451-8470 at 8456, 8460 (US 23931).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2045060177-0203-0178-0180-us-20459', '1107', '2045060177-0203 at 0178, 0180 (US 20459).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'additionally-traits-associated-drivers-are', '1109', 'Additionally, "traits associated with the drivers are consistent with those often mentioned for the cowboy -- masculinity, confidence, strength, determination, independence and skill." In sum,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2072475100-5149-5102-5122-5123-5148', '1110', '2072475100-5149 at 5102, 5122, 5123, 5148 (US 85191).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'continue-be-primary-importance-growth', '1110', '"continue to be of primary importance for the growth of Marlboro." The report opened by discussing'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'key-consumer-insights-including', '1110', '"Key Consumer Insights," including:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'after-discussing-core-values-marlboro', '1110', 'After discussing the "core values of Marlboro Country" -- "Masculinity, Freedom, Adventure,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'limitless-opportunities-self-sufficiency-mastery-destiny', '1110', 'Limitless Opportunities, Self-Sufficiency, Mastery of Destiny, Harmony with Nature" -- the report addressed Marlboro''s "Advertising Challenge":'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-continued-addressing-under-heading', '1110', 'The report continued by addressing, under the heading of "Creative Direction," Marlboro''s'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'advertising-objectives', '1110', '"Advertising Objectives":'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'lb0092389-2414-2391-2394-2396-us-33235', '1111', 'LB0092389-2414 at 2391-2394, 2396 (US 33235) (emphasis in original); 2085298486-8512 at 8488- 8491, 8493 (US 22906).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2-lorillard', '1112', '(2) Lorillard'),
