('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'timothy-k-hoelter-harley-davidson', '1112', 'Timothy K. Hoelter, Harley Davidson Vice President and General Counsel, wrote to Ronald'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'goldbrenner-lorillard-associate-general-counsel', '1112', 'Goldbrenner, Lorillard Associate General Counsel, expressing Harley Davidson''s concern that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'lorillard-s-proposed-upcoming-cigarette', '1112', 'Lorillard''s proposed upcoming cigarette advertising campaign to introduce its new Harley Davidson brand, especially when combined with the low price of the brand, would "recruit underage smokers."'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'hoelter-indicated-harley-davidson-had', '1113', 'Hoelter indicated that Harley Davidson had hired a market research firm specializing in child research to evaluate the Lorillard advertising campaign, and that this firm had concluded that "the campaign will appeal to underaged children." 91384161-4162 (US 54404); 92670418-0419 at 0419'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'us-21760', '1113', '(US 21760).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '92670436-0437-us-57194', '1113', '92670436-0437 (US 57194).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'november-30-1994-stated-one', '1113', 'November 30, 1994 stated that one objective was "[t]o develop a comprehensive Newport Promotion'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'program-which-enhances-image-one', '1114', 'Program which . . . Enhances image as one of the ''cool'' brands." 91945211-5218 at 5216 (US'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '96290861-0869-0869-us-85209', '1115', '96290861-0869 at 0869 (US 85209*).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'newport-cigarettes-captioned-pleasure-fire', '1115', 'Newport cigarettes captioned "Pleasure! Fire It Up!" in newspapers and magazines. Among several treatments, "Pleasure! Fire It Up!" advertising depicted attractive young men and young women smoking cigarettes, often in circumstances involving sports and other physical activities. (no bates)'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'us-11209-no-bates-us', '1115', '(US 11209); (no bates) (US 11247); (no bates) (US 11257); (no bates) (US 11283); (no bates) (US'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '14767-no-bates-us-14637', '1115', '14767); (no bates) (US 14637); (no bates) (US 12477).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '86165773-5775a-5775-us-22207', '1115', '86165773-5775A at 5775 (US 22207).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'creative-strategy-increase-volume-gain', '1116', 'The "Creative Strategy" to increase volume and gain long term growth was:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '98196660-6681-6661-6665-6671-us', '1116', '98196660-6681 at 6661, 6665, 6671 (US 56953). The "Newport 2001 Strategic Plan Overview," dated June 9, 2000, set forth "Marketing Objectives" identical to the year 2000 plan. 99310880-0893 at 0884-0885 (US 57656) (Confidential).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'b-w-designed-its-marketing', '1117', 'B&W designed its marketing campaigns around themes that would exploit these attitudes. 170040977-1001 at 0977 (US 20289); see also (no bates) (US 8013); (no bates) (US 1094); (no bates) (US 10443).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '680092632--2668-2664-2665-us-21693', '1118', '680092632- 2668 at 2664-2665 (US 21693); 170043558-3593 at 3581-3582 (US 20293); 679018003-8278 (US 87928).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '777080491-0522-0491-0500-0508-us', '1118', '777080491-0522 at 0491, 0500, 0508 (US 31585).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'marlboro-menthol-through-contemporary-exploitation', '1120', 'Marlboro Menthol through a contemporary exploitation of the Kool Indy car program." 1760207572942. In 1997 B&W sponsored the H.O.R.D.E. (Horizons of Rock Developing Everywhere) Festival, an annual all-day music festival staged in twenty-eight cities across the United States over the summer. Prior to the H.O.R.D.E. Festival, B&W sponsored the "Extremely Kool Band-to-Band Combat" competitions in ten United States cities "with the grand prize being the opening act on the Second Stage at three H.O.R.D.E. shows." The objectives for the "Extremely Kool Band-to-Band Combat" competitions included "[i]mprov[ing] perceptions of Kool as a popular, up-to-date, leading brand" and capturing names for B&W''s smoker database. 306014279-4279 (US 22102).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '844002422-2437-2432-2434-2437-us', '1121', '844002422-2437 at 2432, 2434, 2437 (US 21921).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'letter-criticized-use-young-female', '1122', 'The letter criticized the use of a young female model in the campaign who "looks like a teenager from head to toe" and the use of billboards. The Governor concluded his letter by requesting that B&W remove "these offensive billboards immediately . . . and immediately halt this campaign." 282208267-8267 (US 22099).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '282204359-4361-4359-4360-us-22211', '1122', '282204359-4361 at 4359-4360 (US 22211).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1999-mri-twelve-plus-study', '1123', '1999 MRI Twelve Plus Study. B&W had placed "B Kool" advertisements in such magazines as Vibe and Sport, which had youth readership (readers between the ages of twelve and seventeen) above 35% based on the 1999 MRI Twelve Plus Study. Edmonson wrote that:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'noted-s-ome-ads-include', '1123', 'He noted that "[s]ome of the ads include visual cues, e.g. tattoos which are currently in vogue among teens. This imagery is likely to appeal to male adolescents." Edmonson also stated that the "B Kool" slogan was more likely to "resonate" with young adolescents than with smokers twenty-one to thirty years old. In response to B&W''s contention that the advertising campaign was intended to target twenty-one to thirty year olds, Edmonson stated'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'b-w-did-not-change', '1123', 'B&W did not change the content of the B Kool campaign in response to the concerns expressed by National Association of Attorneys General ("NAAG"). 282300205-0207 at 0205-0206 (US 20574); Smith WD, 32:20-33:8.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'special-edition-packs-referenced-advertisements', '1124', 'The special edition packs referenced in the advertisements featured the same images of DJs and young people dancing. Also included in the April 2004 edition of Rolling Stone was a Kool Mixx CD/CD-Rom, described in the advertisements as "Your way to experience the sights and sounds of the Soundtrack to the Streets." The CD-Rom contained, among other things, soundtracks by various hip-hop artists, interviews with DJs, and a link to the website www.houseofmenthol.com, which the press release described as a "comprehensive, age-verified website for adult smokers" created as part of the KOOL Mixx campaign. Ivey WD, 28:4- 29:27, 33:1-34:20; ADV1150001-0117 (US 88094); Krugman WD, 116:3-122:7; USX5420003-0008 (US 89164). See http://www.trinketsandtrash.org/featured/koolcampaign.htm.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'maine-attorney-general-chair-tobacco', '1125', 'Maine Attorney General and Chair of the Tobacco Enforcement Committee, in a March 25, 2004 letter to Neil Mellon, wrote, "[t]he advertising images used in this campaign [hip-hop artists, DJ''s, art, and culture] appear to us to hold particular appeal for teenagers." It was also brought to B&W''s attention that individuals were able to gain access to www.houseofmenthol.com, its supposedly "age-verified" website, by providing false information.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '4-r-j-reynolds', '1126', '(4) R.J. Reynolds'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'some-thoughts-about-new-brands', '1126', 'Some Thoughts About New Brands Of Cigarettes For The Youth Market," Claude E. Teague, Jr.,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'assistant-director-research-rjr-set', '1126', 'Assistant Director of Research at RJR, set forth the following strategy for appealing to young people''s desires to smoke popular and peer-approved brands:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '502987407-502987418-7413-us-20708', '1126', '502987407-502987418 at 7413 (US 20708).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '800057286-7321-7299-7302-us-21057', '1127', '800057286-7321 at 7299 at 7302 (US 21057).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'white-paper-then-discussed-how', '1128', 'The White Paper then discussed how Camel could reconfigure its market image in order to appeal to the "peer acceptability and belonging" themes so effectively exploited by Marlboro''s advertising. 506768775-8784 at 8776, 8781-8784 (US 20764).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'overall-plan-rjr-s-billboard', '1129', 'The overall plan for RJR''s billboard efforts was described as "[c]ontinuous, high impact visibility in the most YAS-oriented media available." The overall objective was to: "Assure continuous OOH presence for highest potential Brands, utilizing locations, units and creative executions that are uniquely and singlemindedly relevant to younger adult smokers." The report recommended placing billboards in the areas most likely to be frequented by young adults, including:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '---near-venues-where-rock', '1129', '-- Near venues where rock concerts are regularly held.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-stated-respect-marketing-such', '1129', 'The report stated that, with respect to marketing in such areas, "[t]raditional OOH selection parameters do not necessarily apply! Highly ''daily effective circulation'' not critical -- maybe YAS only in area on weekends -- that''s OK!" 507286174-6181 at 6175-6576, 6178 (US 22051).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'perception-study-declared-soundwaves-program', '1129', 'Perception Study," declared that the Soundwaves Program was:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'march-6-1989-document-produced', '1130', 'A March 6, 1989 document produced from RJR files, titled "1990 New Marketing Ideas," referenced an "Inner-City Black Targeted Brand" that would be a distinctive cigarette brand targeted at the Inner-city Black smoker" and would "leverage the Black consumers'' desire to use products which . . . are more ''potent'' (e.g., Blacks drink malt liquor rather than beer)." An October 18, 1989 RJR marketing research report, titled "Project UT [Uptown] Creative Qualitative Research," stated "Project UT is a new brand targeted to younger adult Black smokers," and described the results of focus group testing conducted in Chicago among eighteen to twenty-four year old African American males and females who had "a high school or less education, and a total household income under $20,000 per year." Only after the then-Secretary of HHS, Dr. Lewis Sullivan, gave a speech condemning Uptown did RJR decide not to bring Uptown to market. Schindler TT, 1/25/05, 10952:4-10953:14; Schindler WD, 112:2-22, 121:19-24; 505925251-5295 at 5253, 5263, 5278 (US 89347); 507297419-7442 at 7438 (US 89351); 507318253-8287 at 8254, 8257 (US 89346).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'leary-pd-united-states-v-2', '1131', 'Leary PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 5/2/02, 60:25-62:23.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'marketing-development-joe-camel-described', '1131', 'marketing. The development of Joe Camel, described below, highlights Defendants'' efforts to market to youth.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '503561565-1570-1567-us-21704-502656424-6660', '1132', '503561565-1570 at 1567 (US 21704); 502656424-6660 (US 87821).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'martin-also-discussed-focus-group', '1133', 'Martin also discussed focus group reactions to advertisements featuring the "French Camel," which was the precursor to the Joe Camel campaign:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '521895554-5555-5554-us-52788-504585737-5757', '1133', '521895554-5555 at 5554 (US 52788); 504585737-5757 at 5738-5739 (US 50628).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1985-memorandum-from-j-s', '1133', '1985 memorandum from J.S. Carpenter, RJR Tobacco International employee, to John Winebrenner about the "Funny French Camel Design" described RJR''s use of the "French Camel" campaign to attract young smokers in France. Carpenter wrote:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'report-indicated-advertising-will-be', '1134', 'The report indicated that "advertising will be developed with the objective of convincing target smokers that by selecting Camel as their usual brand they will project an image that will enhance their acceptance among their peers." 503969238-9242 at 9238 (US 79096).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '506768775-8784-8777-8779-8783-us-20764', '1136', '506768775-8784 at 8777, 8779-8783 (US 20764) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '8590-no-bates-us-9271', '1136', '8590); (no bates) (US 9271); (no bates) (US 8521); (no bates) (US 8835); (no bates) (US 8905); (no bates) (US 1809).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'camel-advertising-test-recommending-rjr', '1136', 'Camel'' Advertising Test" recommending that RJR conduct market research to determine the effectiveness of the "Heroic Camel" advertising campaign, and assure that it was positively received by eighteen to thirty year olds. The "Heroic Camel" campaign showed Joe Camel in a "series of'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'heroic-situations-drawn-from-bigger', '1137', '''heroic'' situations drawn from bigger than life fictional characters," including as a fighter pilot, a foreign legionnaire, "Hollywood," and a detective. These advertisements were run in 1989. 521895566-5570 (US 24813*).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '517161869-1876-1869-us-80669', '1137', '517161869-1876 at 1869 (US 80669).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '517161877-1877-us-80670', '1137', '517161877-1877 (US 80670).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'promotional-items-suggested-report-included', '1138', 'The promotional items suggested by this report included blank audio tapes with Camel logo, a Camel Walkman case and other "entertainment-oriented incentives." Other suggestions included the'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'camel-pocket-game-which-included', '1139', '"Camel pocket game," which included chess, checkers, dominoes, or Parcheesi, all using Camel logos, graphics and visuals. 509216033-6056 at 6035-6036, 6041, 6044-6045 (US 20826).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '507642890-2934-2892-us-22055', '1140', '507642890-2934 at 2892 (US 22055).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '512027239-7240-7240-us-20845', '1140', '512027239-7240 at 7240 (US 20845).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'cigarette-other-tobacco-prices-will', '1142', 'in cigarette and other tobacco prices, and will not try smoking or continue to smoke if cigarette prices rise. Chaloupka WD, 94:23-124:4. Despite that recognition, Defendants continue to use price-based marketing efforts as a key marketing strategy. As a result, price reductions, initiated by the cigarette company Defendants, such as sharply dropping the wholesale price of cigarettes most popular with young people, have reduced the rate of decline in overall cigarette smoking and contributed to the increases in youth smoking incidence and prevalence observed during much of the 1990s. Chaloupka WD, 86:5-87:13.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'from-george-weissman-vice-president', '1144', 'from George Weissman, Vice President of Philip Morris, to Dr. R.N. DuPuis, Philip Morris Scientific Research Director, described the results of a 1956 college survey conducted by Elmo Roper for Philip Morris. In a section of his memorandum titled "The Economics of Cigarettes," Weissman stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2022240073-0075-0074-us-20359', '1145', '2022240073-0075 at 0074 (US 20359).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'johnston-postulated-any-general-increase', '1145', 'Johnston postulated that, with any general increase in cigarette prices, "I would expect a disproportionately large number of Marlboro smokers to quit smoking or reduce daily consumption." 1003285497-5502 at 5497, 5500 (US 20160).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1003478193-8196-8193-8194-us-20175', '1146', '1003478193-8196 at 8193-8194 (US 20175).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'g-iven-evidence-individuals-are', '1146', '"[G]iven the evidence that individuals are considerably less likely to initiate smoking after age 25, it is quite possible the cohort . . . who never begin to smoke as a result of the tax increase would never become regular smokers." 1003478193-8196 at 8195, 8196 (US 20175).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '1003478185-8191-8189-us-35774-2049456635-6650', '1146', '1003478185-8191 at 8189 (US 35774); 2049456635-6650 at 6639 (US 20487).');
INSERT INTO passages (report, section, paragraph_id, page, body) VALUES
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'cigarette-sales-outlined-philip-morris', '1146', 'Cigarette Sales," outlined Philip Morris''s opposition to raising excise taxes on cigarettes despite studies showing that raising cigarette prices was the most effective way to reduce youth initiation and youth smoking. The report reflected Philip Morris''s knowledge that "[t]he main effect of an excise tax increase will be to reduce the number of young people who begin to smoke." Nonetheless,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'philip-morris-continued-vigorously-oppose', '1147', 'Philip Morris continued to vigorously oppose all cigarette excise tax proposals. 2049456670-6694 at 6684 (US 20489).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'handling-excise-tax-increase-johnston', '1147', '"Handling an Excise Tax Increase," Johnston stated that:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2022216179-6180-us-76177', '1147', '2022216179-6180 (US 76177).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '2441-us-21984', '1147', '2441 (US 21984).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'philip-morris-usa-testified', '1147', 'Philip Morris USA, testified that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'morgan-pd-minnesota-v-philip', '1148', 'Morgan PD, Minnesota v. Philip Morris, 9/4/97, 219:23-220:15.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'price-affects-consumption-petch-pd', '1149', 'that price affects consumption. Petch PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 10/12/01, 101:25-102:21.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'product-development-marketing-research-regarding', '1149', 'of Product Development and Marketing Research, regarding "Price Sensitivity By Age" stated that'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '82849666-9667-9666-us-55569', '1150', '82849666-9667 at 9666 (US 55569).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'kool-cigarettes-than-any-its', '1150', 'of Kool cigarettes than any of its other brands, according to Paul Wessel, the Current Divisional Vice President at B&W in charge of value for money premium niche brand and new product development. Wessel PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 3/19/03, 28:17-29:1.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'following-federal-excise-tax-increase', '1150', 'Following Federal Excise Tax Increase," to P.E. Gaylan, a Marketing Research Department employee, Diane Burrows estimated how the cigarette industry would be affected by a federal excise tax increase. The memorandum included data on "starting age patterns," "[s]tarting age," and "new smokers." Burrows estimated that an excise tax increase would result in 1,759,000 "new smokers" lost to the industry. Their potential consumption, if they had smoked ten cigarettes a day, would amount to 605 million cigarettes, or .1% of the industry total. Burrows stated that: "[s]ince the Industry growth rate depends on new smokers, losses in these groups can change the direction of the'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', 'industry-trend-501988846-8849-8846-8846-8848', '1151', 'Industry trend." 501988846-8849 at 8846, 8846-8848 (US 20692); 504630598-0702 at 0701 (US'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '500151647-1647-us-21785', '1151', '500151647-1647 (US 21785).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Tracking Youth Behavior and Preferences Ensures that Marketing and', '503011368-1369-1368-us-20709', '1151', '503011368-1369 at 1368 (US 20709).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'defendants-advertising-promotional-expenses-rose', '1152', 'Defendants'' advertising and promotional expenses rose significantly after the signing of the MSA in November 1998. 1900082-0107 (US 60663).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'advertisements-placed-youth-oriented-magazines', '1155', 'advertisements they placed in youth oriented magazines after signing the MSA. Krugman WD, 124:13-127:4.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'advertisements-publications-where-80-more', '1156', 'advertisements in publications where 80% or more of a magazine''s readership was twenty-one years and older. Philip Morris''s evaluation process was not quantitative. Rather, the Philip Morris Media Department, along with legal counsel, simply made subjective determinations and recommendations for publication placements based upon personal review of the "content" of the publication, including consideration of whether the publication''s editorial content was directed towards adults and whether other products advertised in the publication were for adult consumption. Through this subjective determination process, Philip Morris''s media employees and attorneys would decide whether a publication passed muster under the advertising guidelines as set forth in the industry''s Cigarette Advertising and Promotion Code. Virtually no magazines failed to qualify for placement of Philip Morris cigarette advertisements under Philip Morris''s subjective review process during this period. Camisa PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/28/02, 24:23-27:10, 32:19-33:11, 51:19-52:4, 81:14- 82:16.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'time-philip-morris-continued-advertise', '1157', 'At this time, Philip Morris continued to advertise in many magazines with high youth readership such as Rolling Stone. Id. at 24:23-27-24, 51:19-52:8, 81:14-82:16.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'camisa-provided-examples-such-placements', '1159', 'Camisa provided examples of such placements, including: special impact units (three to four page units that may appear in a publication, as opposed to a single page); the "second" cover; page one (the inside of the front cover and first page); the back cover; or, the center spread in a magazine that is stapled so that a reader naturally opens up to the magazine''s center to see a showcased advertisement. Camisa PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/28/02, 113:6-114:24; 20804998299896 (US 20536). Such placements grab the attention of the reader and have far more impact on his or her buying decisions.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'camisa-pd-united-states-v', '1160', 'Camisa PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/28/02, 111:22-113:5; 2071230813-0888 (US 40404).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'driver-hot-rod-penthouse-vibe', '1160', 'Driver, Hot Rod, Penthouse, Vibe, Stereo Review, Car Craft, Cycle World,4 One cannot help wondering whether this litigation was the best vehicle for attempting to hold Defendants accountable for their indifference to the health of American citizens. In a democracy, it is the body elected by the people, namely Congress, that should step up to the plate and address national issues with such enormous economic, public health, commercial, and social ramifications, rather than the courts which are limited to deciding only the particular case presented to them in litigation. However, this will certainly not be the first, nor the last, time that litigants seek to use the courts and existing legislation to address broad-scale economic and social problems which might be far better and more appropriately grappled with by our elected representatives.Show full note Wheel, POV,'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'motorcyclist-four-wheeler-espn-through', '1160', 'Motorcyclist, Four Wheeler, and ESPN through at least January 2000. Camisa PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/28/02, 149:2-152:6; 2080499829-9896 at 9837 (US 20536).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', '2070748847-8852-8847-us-21819-emphasis', '1161', '2070748847-8852 at 8847 (US 21819*) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'publications-over-15-under-eighteen', '1164', 'publications with over 15% under eighteen readership. Taylor PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/14/02, 95:8-25, 97:5-99:6.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'primarily-subscribed-minors-distributed-minors', '1165', 'primarily subscribed to by minors or distributed to minors. Lorillard''s Media Services Department relied on a computer program designed by an independent outside agency to identify the magazines in which it was not appropriate to place Lorillard advertisements. Lorillard only looked at readership information on people eighteen years old and older in making its determination. Lorillard would then use its "best judgment" based on the information provided by the publications about the readership of people eighteen years of age and older to make a recommendation as to whether or not to advertise in a particular publication. The recommendations were made by Lorillard''s media department in conjunction with its outside advertising agency. The recommendations were then reviewed and considered by Lorillard''s brand group. Lindsley PD, Massachusetts v. Philip Morris, 6/8/98, 65:13-70:17; Lindsley PD, California v. Philip Morris, 6/9/98, 164:17-171:6.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'attorneys-general-naag-b-w', '1167', 'Attorneys General (NAAG), B&W agreed to restrict the placement of the company''s cigarette advertisements to magazines whose under-twenty-one readership did not exceed 15% of the magazine''s total readership. B&W initially relied on information provided by the publishers of the magazines in which it advertised in order to determine whether the under-twenty-one readership of a magazine exceeded 15%. B&W also examined the editorial content of the magazines in which it advertised. Ivey WD, 16:7-16; Ivey TT, 11/16/04, 6118:3-10.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'change-beasley-pd-united-states', '1169', 'change. Beasley PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/25/02, 42:8-15. In the years preceding 2000, RJR''s print placement policy reflected its interpretation of the Cigarette Advertising Code that prohibited cigarette advertising in any magazine that was primarily directed to underage people. RJR limited its advertising to magazines whose readership was at least 50% adult, adult being defined as twenty-one before May 1992, or eighteen after May 1992. Id. at 55:20-58:3.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', '2002-still-current-print-placement', '1171', '2002, this was still the current print placement policy. Beasley PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 6/25/02, 42:4-6, 44:9-15. RJR used both Simmons and MRI data to evaluate magazine placement. Additionally, it considered other factors, specifically editorial content, the other categories of products advertised, and distribution. Blixt PD, United States v. Philip Morris, 10/31/02, 131:24- 132:10, 137:7-15.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', '116-3-122-7-1999-first', '1172', '116:3-122:7. In 1999, the first year after the MSA was signed, RJR increased its media spending on advertising in such magazines. 524941712-1722 (US 87804).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'individuals-send-them-coupons-t-shirts', '1173', 'individuals to send them coupons, t-shirts, sporting goods, mugs, and magazines, all promoting their brand of cigarettes. These mailings were sent to millions of young people for whom Defendants had nothing more than an unverified representation that s/he was over the age of twenty-one.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'philip-morris-1993-philip-morris', '1175', 'Philip Morris. In 1993, Philip Morris sent 71,485 marketing mailings to such individuals, including 48,822 coupons and 28,335 gift or continuity items, such as t-shirts, mugs, and sporting goods. In 1994, Philip Morris sent 94,151 marketing mailings to such individuals, including 44,919 coupons and 31,572 gift or continuity items. In 1995, Philip Morris sent 76,378 marketing mailings to such individuals, including 30,190 coupons and 34,909 gift or continuity items. Id. at 6016-6018.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'pm3000540103-540118-0107-0116-us-88649', '1176', 'PM3000540103-540118 at 0107, 0116 (US 88649) (Confidential). As further stated in its "2004 Original Budget & Five Year Plan Presentation," in order to address the "Critical Issue" of the "Loss of mass marketing" that it faces ahead in 2004-2008, Philip Morris plans a short-term strategy of marketing through packaging onserts, expanded direct mail, and a rewards card that is preloaded with a fixed dollar amount for cigarette purchases, and a long-term strategy of controlled internet access, or "internet sites marketing cigarettes" to include selling cigarettes on-line, or by phone, fax or mail orders. PM3000613782-3913 at 3790, 3801, 3804, 3887 (US 88647).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'whose-ages-have-not-been', '1176', 'whose ages have not been verified through a copy of government-issued identification or public records database:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'orlowsky-wd-60-22-63-22', '1177', 'Orlowsky WD, 60:22-63:22; 82093356-3358 at 3357-3358 (US 22198).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', '25-765-233-individuals-company', '1178', 'of 25,765,233 individuals. The company publicly states that it limits its direct mail marketing to individuals who, at a minimum, self-certify that they are smokers of legal age. As of August 31, 2004, B&W had no government-issued identification age verification or third-party age verification for approximately half of the individuals contained in its direct mail database. Ivey WD, 44:1-45:17; Ivey TT, 11/17/04, 6224:8-6225:25; 469100116-0136 (US 89166) (Confidential); USX5560116- 0119 (US 92039).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'marketing-peggy-carter-personal-relations', '1179', 'Marketing to Peggy Carter of the Personal Relations department describes RJR''s process of age verification for names on its database and states:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'rjr0000000008001178700190551-0551-us-22140-order-be', '1179', 'RJR0000000008001178700190551-0551 (US 22140*). In order to be on its direct mail database, RJR requires self certification that a person is a smoker of a legal age, which must be verified by a Government-issued identification or through a third-party verification.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'brand-imagery-promotional-offers-retail', '1179', 'of brand imagery and promotional offers. At retail stores, Defendants use retail promotion techniques including cash/rebates, free products, display cases to dealers, and special value added offers such as "two-for-one" to consumers, to encourage retailers to create tobacco friendly environments containing enticing displays, competitive prices, and visible point-of-sale advertising. Krugman WD, 129:17-130:11. The result of offering an array of marketing techniques is that convenience stores and gas stations frequented by teenagers are more likely to be tobacco friendly environments because they contain such a profusion of tobacco messages. A recent study funded by the Robert Wood Johnson Foundation examined the use of advertising and promotion in such stores and concluded that retail environments, such as convenience stores and gas retailers frequented by teenagers heavily promote tobacco use. Id.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'report-further-noted-philip-morris', '1182', 'The report further noted that Philip Morris''s product displays were most effective at driving visibility:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', '2073970827-0848-0831-0832-0838-us', '1182', '2073970827-0848 at 0831, 0832, 0838 (US 43390).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', '2063018737-8739-8737-us-85164', '1184', '2063018737-8739 at 8737 (US 85164).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'youth', '1186', 'youth.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'competition-events-scheduled-major-united', '1187', 'Competition events were scheduled in major United States cities such as New York, Chicago, Detroit, and Los Angeles. "Communication Vehicles" used to publicize the Competition included an 800 number, radio spots, pack sleeves, and retail tie-ins. B&W continued to sponsor the Kool Mixx DJ Competition in 2002 and 2003. 432210032-0067 at 0036, 0038, 0047 (US 22226); ARU6432538-2543 (US78267).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'band-event-held-park-west', '1188', 'Band" event held at Park West Concert Hall in Chicago on November 11, 2000 without being asked for any identification. Inside the Concert Hall were "pole banners with the Lucky Strike Band to Band tag-line" as well as additional banners and signs. Desandre described how, while he was filling out a form to receive a free CD, a Lucky Strike staff member "threw me a pack of Lucky Strike cigarettes . . . she did not ask me if I was 21 or a smoker. She also did not ask for my id. Beth Crehan was also not asked if she was 21 or a smoker. Beth was also not asked for id." 98600272- 0273 (US 22212).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'result-millions-youth-watching-these', '1188', 'a result, millions of youth watching these events are exposed to Defendants'' cigarette marketing imagery.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'commerce-subcommittee-health-environment-radio', '1190', 'Commerce, Subcommittee on Health and Environment that "radio and television exposure is not a motivating consideration for Reynolds in deciding whether to sponsor an event or a vehicle participating in an event." 509321275-1290 (US 21993). However, Susan Ivey, President and CEO of Reynolds American, acknowledged that one of the benefits of brand sponsorship of televised sporting events is exposure of the brand name on television. Ivey WD, 48:6- 49:4.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'philip-morris-planned-d-ominate', '1192', 'Philip Morris planned to "[d]ominate retail environment thirty days prior to the race with three tier wave promotion . . . [and] Display racing POS for 30 days prior to the race." The document also noted that the Marlboro Pole Award "provides Philip Morris with . . . Year-long visibility at all venues." 2060138575-8585 at 8577, 8580, 8581 (US 24004).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 'philip-morris-evaluated-its-racing', '1193', 'Philip Morris evaluated its racing sponsorships and adjusted its "marketing strategy for motorsports" going forward. To the question of whether Philip Morris should remain in motorsports sponsorships, the answer was: "Yes: It enables us to reach millions of our target market with TV media coverage, and is particularly important in restricted markets." The identified objectives were: (1) to "Regain momentum in the hearts and minds of our target market -- young adult smokers under 25"; and (2) to "look at current and new program opportunities to extend our reach with starters and young adult smokers." One specific Formula 1, a European racing league, marketing strategy was to create a Formula 1 "team of young talent which is not necessarily a winning team, more rebellious, fun, daredevil, more easily identifiable with the young adult target market." The team would feature "[a]nti-establishment gear (jeans/boots)" and a "[c]razy car design." 2501058650-8680 at 8657- 8658, 8661 (US 21702).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Marketing Successfully Reaches Youth', 't-shirts-mugs-lighters----retail', '1193', 'as t-shirts, mugs, or lighters -- at retail and via direct mail.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Youth Smoking Prevention Programs Are Not Designed to', 'prevent-youth-smoking-corporate-programs', '1194', 'to prevent youth smoking, and the corporate programs they have adopted to achieve those goals. MNAT00280070-0070 (US 21724). Defendants'' "youth programs" and youth smoking prevention efforts are not only minimally funded -- given the vast sums they spend on marketing and promotion to youth -- and understaffed both qualitatively and quantitatively, but no efforts have been made to validate their effectiveness amongst the total population. Biglan WD, 381:5-17.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Youth Smoking Prevention Programs Are Not Designed to', 'defendants-have-not-adopted-implemented', '1195', 'Defendants have not adopted or implemented any of these four strategies. Id. at 386:7-398:16, 401:12-411:8; Chaloupka WD, 30:15-32:20.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Youth Smoking Prevention Programs Are Not Designed to', '94691840-1858-us-87874-biglan-wd', '1199', '94691840-1858 (US 87874); Biglan WD, 409:5-18.'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Youth Smoking Prevention Programs Are Not Designed to', 'timn0164421-4424-4423-us-34445-emphasis', '1203', 'TIMN0164421-4424 at 4423 (US 34445*) (emphasis in original).'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Youth Smoking Prevention Programs Are Not Designed to', 'additionally-document-stated', '1203', 'Additionally, the document stated:'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants'' Youth Smoking Prevention Programs Are Not Designed to', '2044046017-6022-6021-6022-us-66716', '1203', '2044046017-6022 at 6021-6022 (US 66716).'),
