('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Undertook Joint Efforts to Undermine and Discredit the', 'tobacco-chairman-tony-garrett-called', '1303', 'Tobacco Chairman Tony Garrett called Hugh Cullman, then Executive Vice President of Philip Morris Incorporated and President of Philip Morris International, to explore whether several of the world''s largest manufacturers, including Philip Morris, BATCo, Reynolds, Reemtsma, and Rothmans "might be prepared to meet discreetly to develop a defensive smoking and health strategy for major markets such as the UK, Germany, Canada, US and possibly others." 2025025286-5286 (US'),
('us-v-philip-morris', 'Defendants Undertook Joint Efforts to Undermine and Discredit the', 'stated-concern-companies-countries-would', '1304', 'The stated concern was that "the companies and countries would be picked off one by one and that the Domino theory would impact on all of us." 2025025286-5286 (US 20407).'),
